PathwayData.put("data/reading_writing/units/L04U3.json",{"strand":"reading_writing","level":4,"cefr":"A2b","unit":3,"theme":"Sports and Teamwork","essential_question":"What makes a team successful?","schema_version":"1.0","core_words":["football","coach","player","captain","practice","score","goal","match","cheer","effort","respect","trophy","train","champion"],"recycled_words":["run","jump","kick","team","friend","proud","nervous","opinion","reason","problem","because","so","finally"],"rubrics":[{"id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","title":"Analytic writing rubric","traits":[{"name":"Ideas","name_ar":"الأفكار","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear, interesting and fully developed with strong details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة وممتعة ومدعومة بتفاصيل قوية."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear and have enough details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة ومعها تفاصيل كافية."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"My main idea is there but needs more details.","descriptor_ar":"فكرتي الرئيسية موجودة لكنها تحتاج إلى تفاصيل أكثر."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"My ideas are unclear or very few.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري غير واضحة أو قليلة جدًا."}]},{"name":"Organization","name_ar":"التنظيم","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Clear beginning, middle and end; ideas flow with linking words.","descriptor_ar":"بداية ووسط ونهاية واضحة، والأفكار مترابطة بكلمات الربط."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Clear order with some linking words.","descriptor_ar":"ترتيب واضح مع بعض كلمات الربط."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Some order, but parts are mixed up.","descriptor_ar":"يوجد بعض الترتيب لكن بعض الأجزاء غير مرتبة."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Ideas are not in order.","descriptor_ar":"الأفكار غير مرتبة."}]},{"name":"Vocabulary","name_ar":"المفردات","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"I use exact, varied words, including new unit words, correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات دقيقة ومتنوعة، منها كلمات الوحدة الجديدة، بشكل صحيح."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"I use some new words correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم بعض الكلمات الجديدة بشكل صحيح."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"I use simple words; some are repeated or wrong.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات بسيطة، وبعضها مكرر أو غير صحيح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"I use very few words; the meaning is hard to understand.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات قليلة جدًا ويصعب فهم المعنى."}]},{"name":"Sentence fluency","name_ar":"سلاسة الجمل","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My sentences are complete, varied in length and easy to read aloud.","descriptor_ar":"جملي كاملة ومتنوعة الطول وسهلة القراءة بصوت عالٍ."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Most sentences are complete, with some variety.","descriptor_ar":"معظم جملي كاملة مع بعض التنويع."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Many sentences are short or start the same way.","descriptor_ar":"كثير من جملي قصيرة أو تبدأ بالطريقة نفسها."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Sentences are incomplete or run together.","descriptor_ar":"جملي ناقصة أو متداخلة."}]},{"name":"Conventions","name_ar":"قواعد الكتابة","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Capitals, punctuation, spelling and grammar are almost always correct.","descriptor_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة وعلامات الترقيم والإملاء والقواعد صحيحة دائمًا تقريبًا."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"A few mistakes that do not affect meaning.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء قليلة لا تؤثر في المعنى."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Several mistakes; the meaning is sometimes unclear.","descriptor_ar":"عدة أخطاء، والمعنى أحيانًا غير واضح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Many mistakes make it hard to read.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء كثيرة تجعل القراءة صعبة."}]}]}],"lessons":[{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS1","title":"Word Power: Sports and Teamwork","lesson_type":"vocabulary","objectives":["read, say and use 14 words about sports and teamwork and 3 Tier 2 words (cooperate, encourage, perspective)","understand and use sports phrasal verbs (warm up, cool down, give up, join in, cheer on, kick off)","describe what makes a good team player"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة ونطق واستخدام 14 كلمة عن الرياضة والعمل الجماعي و3 كلمات أكاديمية.","فهم الأفعال المركبة الرياضية واستخدامها.","وصف صفات اللاعب الجيد في الفريق."],"success_criteria":["I can read and use the sports words in sentences.","I can explain what a sports phrasal verb means.","I can describe a good team player with three words."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع قراءة كلمات الرياضة واستخدامها في جمل.","أستطيع شرح معنى الفعل المركب الرياضي.","أستطيع وصف لاعب الفريق الجيد بثلاث كلمات."],"map_area":"Vocabulary: Acquisition and Use","vocabulary":[{"word":"football","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfʊtbɔl/","definition":"a game where two teams kick a ball and try to get it into a net","arabic":"كرة القدم","example":"Omar plays football every afternoon.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"coach","pos":"noun","ipa":"/koʊtʃ/","definition":"a person who trains a team or a player","arabic":"مدرّب","example":"Our coach shows us how to pass the ball.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"player","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpleɪər/","definition":"a person who plays a sport or a game","arabic":"لاعب","example":"Each team has eleven players.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"captain","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkæptən/","definition":"the leader of a team","arabic":"قائد الفريق","example":"Omar is the captain of our team.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"practice","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/ˈpræktɪs/","definition":"doing something again and again to get better","arabic":"تدريب / يتدرّب","example":"We have football practice on Tuesdays.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"score","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/skɔr/","definition":"to get a goal or a point; the number of points","arabic":"يسجّل / النتيجة","example":"Hamza scored two goals. The score was 2–1.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"goal","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɡoʊl/","definition":"the net you kick the ball into; a point in football","arabic":"مرمى / هدف","example":"The ball flew into the goal.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V07","tier":"core"},{"word":"match","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mætʃ/","definition":"a sports game between two teams or players","arabic":"مباراة","example":"The match starts at four o'clock.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V08","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V08","tier":"core"},{"word":"cheer","pos":"verb","ipa":"/tʃɪr/","definition":"to shout to show you are happy or to help a team","arabic":"يهتف / يشجّع","example":"The fans cheered for their team.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V09","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V09","tier":"core"},{"word":"effort","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛfərt/","definition":"hard work to do something","arabic":"جهد","example":"The team won because of their great effort.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V10","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V10","tier":"core"},{"word":"respect","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/rɪˈspɛkt/","definition":"showing that you think someone is important; to treat people well","arabic":"احترام / يحترم","example":"Players shake hands to show respect.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V11","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V11","tier":"core"},{"word":"trophy","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtroʊfi/","definition":"a cup or prize for the winner","arabic":"كأس / جائزة","example":"The captain lifted the trophy.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V12","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V12","tier":"core"},{"word":"train","pos":"verb","ipa":"/treɪn/","definition":"to practice a sport to get better and stronger","arabic":"يتدرّب","example":"The runners train every morning.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V13","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V13","tier":"core"},{"word":"champion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃæmpiən/","definition":"the winner of a competition","arabic":"بطل","example":"Our school became the champion this year.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V14","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V14","tier":"core"},{"word":"cooperate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/koʊˈɑpəreɪt/","definition":"to work together to do something","arabic":"يتعاون","example":"Players cooperate to score a goal.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V15","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V15","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"encourage","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɪnˈkɝɪdʒ/","definition":"to give someone hope and help them try","arabic":"يشجّع","example":"Good captains encourage their players.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V16","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V16","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"perspective","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pərˈspɛktɪv/","definition":"the way one person sees or thinks about something","arabic":"وجهة نظر / منظور","example":"From the coach's perspective, the team played well.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V17","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V17","tier":"tier2"}],"explanation":{"text":"A **phrasal verb** is a verb + a small word like **up, down, in, on, off**. Together they make a **new meaning**. *Give* means to hand something to someone, but ***give up*** means **stop trying**!\n\nSports phrasal verbs: **warm up** (do easy exercise before sport), **cool down** (do slow exercise after sport), **give up** (stop trying), **join in** (start to take part), **cheer on** (shout to help someone win), **kick off** (start a football match), **work out** (do exercise to get fit).\n\nSteps: (1) Find the **verb + small word**. (2) Don't translate the words one by one. (3) Use the **context** (the other words in the sentence) to guess the meaning. (4) Check with the word list.","examples":["*Before the match, we **warm up** by jogging and stretching.* = do easy exercise first.","*After the race, the runners **cool down** by walking slowly.* = do slow exercise after sport.","*Sami was losing, but he didn't **give up**.* = he did not stop trying.","*Adam asked, \"Can I **join in**?\" and the boys passed him the ball.* = take part.","*Our families came to **cheer** us **on**.* = shout to help us win.","*The final match **kicks off** at 4 p.m.* = starts.","*My uncle **works out** at the gym three times a week.* = exercises.","Opposites: **warm up** ↔ **cool down**; **give up** ↔ **keep going**.","A good team player **cooperates**, **encourages** others, shows **respect** and never **gives up**."],"common_errors":["✗ We warm before the match. → ✓ We warm up before the match. (Don't forget the small word **up**.)","✗ He gave up to run. → ✓ He gave up running. (**give up** + -ing.)","✗ I want to join. → ✓ I want to join in. (**join in** = take part in an activity.)","✗ The match kicks at 4. → ✓ The match kicks off at 4. (**kick off** = start.)","✗ We cheer them. → ✓ We cheer them on. (**cheer someone on** = help them with shouts.)","✗ The team are champion. → ✓ The team is the champion. (Use **the champion**.)","✗ He make a big effort. → ✓ He makes a big effort. (One person → **makes**.)"],"arabic":"الفعل المركب (phrasal verb) فعل + كلمة صغيرة مثل up أو down أو in أو on أو off، ويصبح له معنى جديد.\n\nwarm up = إحماء قبل الرياضة، cool down = تهدئة بعدها، give up = يستسلم، join in = يشارك، cheer on = يشجّع، kick off = تبدأ المباراة.\n\nلا تترجم الكلمات كلمة كلمة؛ استخدم السياق لتخمين المعنى ثم تحقق من قائمة الكلمات.\n\nاللاعب الجيد يتعاون ويشجّع غيره ويحترم الآخرين ولا يستسلم."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Welcome to the stadium! Today: sports and teamwork. I'm Omar, the captain!","on_screen":"Sports and Teamwork ⚽","visual":"Omar in his green sports jacket waves on a school field; Saqr the falcon flies over the goal."},{"time":"00:20–01:10","narration":"Coach, players, captain… practice, train, match, goal, score! Fans cheer, and the champion lifts the trophy!","on_screen":"coach · player · captain · practice · train · match · goal · score · cheer · trophy · champion","visual":"Quick scenes of practice, a match, a goal, fans cheering and a team lifting a cup."},{"time":"01:10–02:10","narration":"Phrasal verbs! Warm up before, cool down after. Never give up! Join in, cheer on, kick off!","on_screen":"verb + up / down / in / on / off","visual":"Each phrasal verb appears with a mini action clip."},{"time":"02:10–02:40","narration":"A good team player cooperates, encourages others and shows respect.","on_screen":"cooperate · encourage · respect · effort","visual":"Players pass the ball, high-five and shake hands."},{"time":"02:40–03:00","narration":"Everyone has a different perspective – but one team, one goal!","on_screen":"perspective 👀","visual":"The same goal seen from the goalkeeper's view and from the fans' view."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا بكم في الملعب! اليوم: الرياضة والعمل الجماعي. أنا عمر، قائد الفريق!","مدرب، لاعبون، قائد… تدريب، مباراة، هدف، نتيجة! الجمهور يهتف، والبطل يرفع الكأس!","الأفعال المركبة! إحماء قبل، وتهدئة بعد. لا تستسلم أبدًا! شارك، وشجّع، ولتبدأ المباراة!","اللاعب الجيد يتعاون ويشجّع غيره ويُظهر الاحترام.","لكل شخص وجهة نظر مختلفة… لكن فريق واحد وهدف واحد!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, energetic male sports commentator, speed 0.90. Omar adds comments as the captain."},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","instructions_ar":"اختر الكلمة الصحيحة.","items":[{"q":"The person who trains our football team is the ___.","answer":"coach","explanation":"Coach.","explanation_ar":"المدرب.","options":["coach","trophy","goal","match"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"The leader of the team wears an armband. He is the ___.","answer":"captain","explanation":"Captain.","explanation_ar":"القائد.","options":["champion","captain","player","fan"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"The winners lifted a shiny gold ___.","answer":"trophy","explanation":"Trophy.","explanation_ar":"كأس.","options":["effort","practice","score","trophy"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Hamza kicked the ball into the net. He ___ a goal!","answer":"scored","explanation":"Score.","explanation_ar":"سجّل.","options":["cheered","trained","scored","respected"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Thousands of fans ___ loudly when their team won.","answer":"cheered","explanation":"Cheer.","explanation_ar":"هتفوا.","options":["cheered","trained","scored","practiced"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"The players shook hands after the game to show ___.","answer":"respect","explanation":"Respect.","explanation_ar":"الاحترام.","options":["trophy","practice","respect","goal"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS1-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Sports phrasal verbs. Choose.","instructions_ar":"الأفعال المركبة الرياضية: اختر.","items":[{"q":"*Before the race, we jog and stretch to ___.*","answer":"warm up","explanation":"Before sport.","explanation_ar":"الإحماء.","options":["give up","warm up","cool down","kick off"],"dok":1,"skill":"phrasal verbs","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Sami was tired, but he did not **give up**.* *Give up* means ___.","answer":"stop trying","explanation":"Context.","explanation_ar":"يستسلم.","options":["stop trying","start the game","hand the ball to someone","warm up"],"dok":2,"skill":"phrasal verbs","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*The final match **kicks off** at four o'clock.* *Kicks off* means ___.","answer":"starts","explanation":"Context.","explanation_ar":"تبدأ.","options":["ends","kicks the ball out","gets cancelled","starts"],"dok":2,"skill":"phrasal verbs","stage":"guided"},{"q":"After the match, the players walked slowly to ___.","answer":"cool down","explanation":"After sport.","explanation_ar":"التهدئة.","options":["warm up","kick off","join in","cool down"],"dok":1,"skill":"phrasal verbs","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*Our families came to the stadium to **cheer** us **on**.* What did they do?","answer":"They shouted to help us win.","explanation":"Context.","explanation_ar":"شجّعونا بالهتاف.","options":["They played in the match.","They went home early.","They shouted to help us win.","They gave us the trophy."],"dok":2,"skill":"phrasal verbs","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence uses *join in* correctly?","answer":"Adam asked if he could join in the basketball game.","explanation":"join in = take part.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Adam joined in the ball to the net.","Adam asked if he could join in the basketball game.","Adam join in yesterday the trophy.","Adam joined in tired after practice."],"dok":3,"skill":"phrasal verbs","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS1-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Use the word bank.","instructions_ar":"استخدم بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"Good players ________ with each other and pass the ball.","answer":"cooperate","explanation":"Work together.","explanation_ar":"يتعاونون.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"The captain said, \"You can do it!\" to ________ his teammates.","answer":"encourage","explanation":"Give hope.","explanation_ar":"يشجّع.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"From the goalkeeper's ________, the ball came very fast.","answer":"perspective","explanation":"The way one person sees it.","explanation_ar":"وجهة نظر.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"The team won because everyone made a big ________.","answer":"effort","explanation":"Hard work.","explanation_ar":"جهد.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Our school became the ________ of the football league.","answer":"champion","explanation":"Winner.","explanation_ar":"البطل.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"We have football ________ every Tuesday after school.","answer":"practice","explanation":"Training.","explanation_ar":"تدريب.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS1-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write with the new words.","instructions_ar":"اكتب باستخدام الكلمات الجديدة.","items":[{"q":"Write what you do before and after sport. Use *warm up* and *cool down*.","answer":"Before football, I warm up by jogging. After the match, I cool down by walking slowly.","explanation":"Two phrasal verbs.","explanation_ar":"فعلان مركبان.","dok":2,"skill":"phrasal verbs","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write about a time you did not give up.","answer":"I couldn't swim at first, but I didn't give up, and now I can swim across the pool.","explanation":"give up.","explanation_ar":"give up.","dok":2,"skill":"connect","stage":"production"},{"q":"Describe a good team player with three unit words.","answer":"A good team player cooperates, encourages others and shows respect.","explanation":"Three words.","explanation_ar":"ثلاث كلمات.","dok":2,"skill":"describe","stage":"production"},{"q":"What makes a team successful? Give one reason.","answer":"A team is successful when players cooperate, because no one can win alone.","explanation":"Opinion + reason.","explanation_ar":"رأي + سبب.","dok":3,"skill":"reasoning","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Phrasal Verb Penalty Shoot-Out","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Penalty shoot-out: a phrasal verb appears above the goal; the child taps the ball to shoot at one of four meanings in the net. Correct shots score; wrong ones are saved by Saqr the falcon goalkeeper.","Two teams line up like a penalty shoot-out.","The teacher reads a sentence with a phrasal verb.","The player chooses the correct meaning card and says it.","Correct = the player throws the paper ball at the goal for a bonus point.","After five kicks each, the team with more goals wins."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Which word means *the winner of a competition*?","answer":"champion","explanation":"Champion.","explanation_ar":"بطل.","options":["coach","player","champion","practice"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*Players **cooperate** to win.* *Cooperate* means ___.","answer":"work together","explanation":"Cooperate.","explanation_ar":"يتعاونون.","options":["fight","go home","work together","shout"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"A sports game between two teams is a ___.","answer":"match","explanation":"Match.","explanation_ar":"مباراة.","options":["trophy","coach","goal","match"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"What do you do when you *warm up*?","answer":"easy exercise before sport","explanation":"warm up.","explanation_ar":"الإحماء قبل الرياضة.","options":["slow exercise after sport","easy exercise before sport","stop trying","lift a trophy"],"dok":1,"skill":"phrasal verbs"},{"q":"Which sentence about the tired runner is correct?","answer":"The runner was tired, but she did not give up.","explanation":"give up.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["The runner was tired, but she did not give up.","The runner was tired, but she did not give.","The runner was tired, but she gave up to run.","The runner was tired, but she did not gave up."],"dok":2,"skill":"phrasal verbs"},{"q":"*The captain **encouraged** the new player.* What did he do?","answer":"He gave him hope and helped him try.","explanation":"Encourage.","explanation_ar":"شجّعه.","options":["He gave him hope and helped him try.","He took his ball.","He sent him home.","He scored for him."],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which is the OPPOSITE of *warm up* in sports?","answer":"cool down","explanation":"Opposite.","explanation_ar":"cool down.","options":["join in","kick off","cheer on","cool down"],"dok":2,"skill":"phrasal verbs"},{"q":"*From the fans' **perspective**, the goal was perfect.* *Perspective* means ___.","answer":"the way someone sees something","explanation":"Perspective.","explanation_ar":"وجهة نظر.","options":["a kind of ball","the end of the match","the way someone sees something","a sports shoe"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Why is it hard to guess a phrasal verb from its words alone?","answer":"Together the words make a new meaning.","explanation":"New meaning.","explanation_ar":"لأن معناه جديد.","options":["Together the words make a new meaning.","Phrasal verbs are always long.","They have no verbs.","They are only used in football."],"dok":3,"skill":"strategy"},{"q":"Which player shows the BEST teamwork?","answer":"Faris passes to a teammate who has a better chance to score.","explanation":"Teamwork.","explanation_ar":"التمرير لزميل.","options":["Faris keeps the ball and never passes.","Faris passes to a teammate who has a better chance to score.","Faris shouts at a teammate who missed.","Faris leaves the field when his team is losing."],"dok":3,"skill":"apply"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'football': children playing football on a school field"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'coach': a coach with a whistle and a clipboard"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'player': a boy in a football shirt"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'captain': a player with a captain's armband"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'practice': players doing drills with cones"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'score': a scoreboard showing 2–1"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'goal': a ball in a football net"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V08","prompt":"Picture for the word 'match': two teams on a field at the start of a game"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V09","prompt":"Picture for the word 'cheer': fans cheering with flags"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V10","prompt":"Picture for the word 'effort': a tired but smiling runner"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V11","prompt":"Picture for the word 'respect': two players shaking hands after a match"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V12","prompt":"Picture for the word 'trophy': a shiny gold cup"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V13","prompt":"Picture for the word 'train': children running laps on a track"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V14","prompt":"Picture for the word 'champion': a team holding up a cup on a podium"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V15","prompt":"Picture for the word 'cooperate': players passing the ball to each other"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V16","prompt":"Picture for the word 'encourage': a captain patting a teammate on the back"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V17","prompt":"Picture for the word 'perspective': two children looking at the same ball from different sides"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-01","prompt":"A school football team with friends cheering."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-02","prompt":"Children acting out sports phrasal verbs."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS1-03","prompt":"Players showing respect and encouragement."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V01","script":"football. Omar plays football every afternoon."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V02","script":"coach. Our coach shows us how to pass the ball."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V03","script":"player. Each team has eleven players."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V04","script":"captain. Omar is the captain of our team."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V05","script":"practice. We have football practice on Tuesdays."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V06","script":"score. Hamza scored two goals. The score was 2–1."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V07","script":"goal. The ball flew into the goal."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V08","script":"match. The match starts at four o'clock."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V09","script":"cheer. The fans cheered for their team."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V10","script":"effort. The team won because of their great effort."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V11","script":"respect. Players shake hands to show respect."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V12","script":"trophy. The captain lifted the trophy."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V13","script":"train. The runners train every morning."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V14","script":"champion. Our school became the champion this year."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V15","script":"cooperate. Players cooperate to score a goal."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V16","script":"encourage. Good captains encourage their players."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-V17","script":"perspective. From the coach's perspective, the team played well."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS1-VID","script":"Welcome to the stadium! Today: sports and teamwork. I'm Omar, the captain! Coach, players, captain… practice, train, match, goal, score! Fans cheer, and the champion lifts the trophy! Phrasal verbs! Warm up before, cool down after. Never give up! Join in, cheer on, kick off! A good team player cooperates, encourages others and shows respect. Everyone has a different perspective – but one team, one goal!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS2","title":"The Captain's Choice","lesson_type":"close_reading","objectives":["read a realistic story of about 270 words about a captain's important choice","explain a character's choice: what he chose, why he chose it and what happened","find the theme (lesson) of the story and support it with evidence"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة قصة واقعية من نحو 320 كلمة عن قرار مهم لقائد فريق.","شرح قرار الشخصية: ماذا اختارت ولماذا وماذا حدث.","إيجاد مغزى القصة ودعمه بالدليل."],"success_criteria":["I can say what choice the character made.","I can explain why the character made it, using clues from his words, actions and thoughts.","I can state the theme and give evidence."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع قول القرار الذي اتخذته الشخصية.","أستطيع شرح سبب القرار باستخدام أقوال الشخصية وأفعالها وأفكارها.","أستطيع ذكر المغزى وتقديم الدليل."],"map_area":"Literary Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"final","pos":"noun / adjective","ipa":"/ˈfaɪnəl/","definition":"the last game that decides the winner; last","arabic":"النهائي / أخير","example":"Our team played in the final.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"expect","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɛkt/","definition":"to think that something will happen","arabic":"يتوقّع","example":"Everyone expected Omar to take the penalty.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"referee","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌrɛfəˈri/","definition":"the person who makes sure players follow the rules","arabic":"حكم","example":"The referee blew his whistle.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"penalty","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɛnəlti/","definition":"a free kick at the goal because of a foul","arabic":"ركلة جزاء","example":"Sami took the penalty.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"crowd","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kraʊd/","definition":"a large group of people together","arabic":"حشد / جمهور","example":"The crowd went wild.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"dive","pos":"verb","ipa":"/daɪv/","definition":"to jump forward or sideways with your arms first","arabic":"يقفز / يغطس","example":"The goalkeeper dived to the left.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"believe in","pos":"verb phrase","ipa":"/bɪˈliv ɪn/","definition":"to feel sure that someone can do something","arabic":"يثق بـ / يؤمن بقدرة","example":"\"I believe in you,\" said Omar.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"In many stories, a character makes an **important choice**. To understand it, ask three questions: **What did the character choose? Why did he choose it? What happened because of the choice?**\n\nFind the **why** in the character's **words** (what he says), **actions** (what he does) and **thoughts or memories** (what he remembers). These clues show his **motivation** – the reason inside him.\n\nThe **theme** is the **lesson** the story teaches. It is not just what happened. Write it as a sentence about life: ***A great leader helps others succeed.*** Then support it with **evidence** from the story.","examples":["**What:** Omar chose to give the penalty to Sami.","**Why (memory):** *Omar remembered all the afternoons when Sami had stayed after practice.*","**Why (words):** *\"You've practiced this more than any of us… I believe in you.\"*","**Why (action):** *Omar … holding out the ball.* – he really wants Sami to take it.","**Result:** *The ball flew to the right – into the net!* The team won, and Sami felt proud.","**Other characters:** *Mr. Khalid … nodded slowly.* – the coach agrees with the choice.","**Theme:** ***A great captain helps others succeed, not only himself.***","**Evidence for the theme:** *\"A good player scores goals… A great captain helps others score them.\"*","Not a theme: *Sami scored a goal.* (That is an event, not a lesson.)"],"common_errors":["✗ The theme is football. → ✓ The theme is: a great leader helps others succeed. (Football is the **topic**; the theme is a **lesson**.)","✗ Omar gave the ball because he was tired. → ✓ Omar gave the ball because Sami had practiced hard. (Use **evidence**, not guesses.)","✗ Giving only one clue. → ✓ Use words, actions and memories. (More clues = stronger answer.)","✗ Omar give the ball to Sami. → ✓ Omar gave the ball to Sami. (Past tense: **gave**.)","✗ Sami was shaking his hands. → ✓ Sami's hands were shaking. (The hands shook by themselves.)","✗ The crowd were wild. → ✓ The crowd went wild. (Idiom: **went wild** = became very excited.)"],"arabic":"في كثير من القصص تتخذ الشخصية قرارًا مهمًا. اسأل: ماذا اختارت؟ لماذا؟ وماذا حدث بسبب القرار؟\n\nابحث عن السبب في أقوال الشخصية وأفعالها وأفكارها وذكرياتها؛ فهي تُظهر دافعها الداخلي.\n\nالمغزى هو الدرس الذي تعلّمه القصة، ويُكتب جملةً عن الحياة، مثل: القائد العظيم يساعد الآخرين على النجاح.\n\nالموضوع هو كرة القدم، أما المغزى فهو درس عن الحياة؛ وادعمه دائمًا بدليل من النص."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"The final match. 1–1. Two minutes left. What would YOU do?","on_screen":"The Captain's Choice ⚽","visual":"A scoreboard flashes 1–1 and a clock shows 88:00."},{"time":"00:20–01:50","narration":"It was the final match of the school football cup…","on_screen":"(story)","visual":"Animated story: the foul, Omar picks up the ball, a flashback of Sami practicing alone, the penalty, the goal and the celebration."},{"time":"01:50–02:20","narration":"What did Omar choose? Why? What happened?","on_screen":"What? · Why? · Result?","visual":"Three boxes fill with the answers and evidence."},{"time":"02:20–02:45","narration":"The theme is a lesson about life: A great captain helps others succeed.","on_screen":"Theme = lesson 💡","visual":"Mr. Khalid shakes Omar's hand; the theme sentence appears."},{"time":"02:45–03:00","narration":"Who helps YOU succeed? Who can you help?","on_screen":"Think about it 🤔","visual":"Children high-five in a classroom."}],"captions_ar":["المباراة النهائية. 1–1. بقيت دقيقتان. ماذا كنت ستفعل؟","كانت المباراة النهائية لكأس المدرسة لكرة القدم…","ماذا اختار عمر؟ لماذا؟ وماذا حدث؟","المغزى درس عن الحياة: القائد العظيم يساعد الآخرين على النجاح.","من يساعدك على النجاح؟ ومن تستطيع أن تساعد؟"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm male storyteller, speed 0.90. Different voices for Omar, Sami and Mr. Khalid."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Captain's Choice","body":"It was the final match of the school football cup. Andalus School was playing against Al-Noor School, and the score was 1–1. Only two minutes were left.\n\nOmar, the team captain, wiped his face with the sleeve of his green jacket. All year, he had scored more goals than anyone else on the team. Everyone expected him to win the trophy for them.\n\nSuddenly, a player from Al-Noor tripped Sami near the goal. The referee blew his whistle. \"Penalty!\" he shouted. The crowd jumped to their feet.\n\nOmar picked up the ball. Then he looked at Sami. Sami was sitting on the grass and rubbing his knee, but he was not badly hurt. Omar remembered all the afternoons when Sami had stayed after practice. While the others went home, Sami kicked penalty after penalty at the empty goal. He missed many, but he never gave up. Still, he had never scored in a real match.\n\n\"Sami,\" Omar said, holding out the ball. \"You take it.\"\n\nSami's eyes grew wide. \"Me? But you're our best player!\"\n\n\"You've practiced this more than any of us,\" Omar said. \"I believe in you.\"\n\nMr. Khalid, the coach, watched from the side. He nodded slowly.\n\nSami placed the ball on the spot. His hands were shaking. He took a deep breath, ran forward and kicked. The goalkeeper dived to the left. The ball flew to the right – into the net!\n\nThe crowd went wild. When the final whistle blew, the players lifted Sami onto their shoulders.\n\nLater, Mr. Khalid shook Omar's hand. \"A good player scores goals,\" he said. \"A great captain helps others score them.\"","word_count":272,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U3-LS2-1","genre":"narrative","role":"main","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[{"word":"referee","definition":"the person who makes sure players follow the rules","arabic":"حكم المباراة"},{"word":"penalty","definition":"a free kick at the goal because of a foul","arabic":"ركلة جزاء"},{"word":"trip","definition":"to make someone fall by catching their foot","arabic":"يُعرقل"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the story. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ القصة واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What was the score with two minutes left?","answer":"1–1","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"1–1.","options":["1–1","2–1","0–0","3–1"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Who was the captain of Andalus School's team?","answer":"Omar","explanation":"Paragraph 2.","explanation_ar":"عمر.","options":["Sami","Mr. Khalid","Hamza","Omar"],"dok":1,"skill":"characters","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why did the referee shout *Penalty!*?","answer":"A player from Al-Noor tripped Sami.","explanation":"Paragraph 3.","explanation_ar":"لأن لاعبًا عرقل سامي.","options":["Omar scored a goal.","A player from Al-Noor tripped Sami.","The match was over.","The crowd was too loud."],"dok":1,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Sami do while the others went home after practice?","answer":"He kicked penalty after penalty at the empty goal.","explanation":"Paragraph 4.","explanation_ar":"تدرّب على ركلات الجزاء.","options":["He went home too.","He watched TV.","He kicked penalty after penalty at the empty goal.","He helped the coach clean the field."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Where did the ball go when Sami kicked it?","answer":"to the right, into the net","explanation":"Paragraph 9.","explanation_ar":"إلى اليمين داخل المرمى.","options":["to the left, into the goalkeeper's hands","to the right, into the net","over the goal","out of the stadium"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did the players do when the final whistle blew?","answer":"They lifted Sami onto their shoulders.","explanation":"Paragraph 10.","explanation_ar":"رفعوا سامي على أكتافهم.","options":["They went home quietly.","They argued with the referee.","They gave the trophy away.","They lifted Sami onto their shoulders."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS2-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: The character's choice and the theme. Choose.","instructions_ar":"قرار الشخصية والمغزى: اختر.","items":[{"q":"What choice did Omar make?","answer":"He gave the penalty to Sami.","explanation":"The choice.","explanation_ar":"أعطى الركلة لسامي.","options":["He gave the penalty to Sami.","He took the penalty himself.","He asked the coach to take it.","He left the field."],"dok":1,"skill":"character's choice","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which MEMORY helped Omar decide?","answer":"Sami staying after practice to kick penalties","explanation":"Paragraph 4.","explanation_ar":"تدريب سامي بعد الحصص.","options":["his first trophy","a match against Al-Noor last year","Sami staying after practice to kick penalties","his green jacket"],"dok":2,"skill":"motivation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What do Omar's words *I believe in you* show?","answer":"He trusts Sami.","explanation":"Words → feelings.","explanation_ar":"يثق بسامي.","options":["He is angry with Sami.","He wants to go home.","He is tired.","He trusts Sami."],"dok":2,"skill":"character traits","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What does *Mr. Khalid … nodded slowly* tell us?","answer":"The coach agreed with Omar's choice.","explanation":"Action → meaning.","explanation_ar":"المدرب وافق.","options":["The coach was sleepy.","The coach agreed with Omar's choice.","The coach wanted Omar to take the kick.","The coach was angry."],"dok":2,"skill":"inference","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which word BEST describes Omar as a captain?","answer":"generous","explanation":"He gave his chance away.","explanation_ar":"كريم / يؤثر غيره.","options":["selfish","lazy","generous","shy"],"dok":2,"skill":"character traits","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What is the THEME of *The Captain's Choice*?","answer":"A great leader helps others succeed.","explanation":"Lesson, not event.","explanation_ar":"القائد العظيم يساعد غيره على النجاح.","options":["Football is a fun game.","A great leader helps others succeed.","Sami scored a goal.","Referees blow whistles."],"dok":3,"skill":"theme","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS2-A3","type":"highlight","stage":"freer","instructions":"Find the evidence: Find the evidence.","instructions_ar":"ابحث عن الدليل.","items":[{"q":"Underline the sentence that shows Sami never stopped trying.","answer":"He missed many, but he never gave up.","explanation":"Never gave up.","explanation_ar":"لم يستسلم.","evidence":"He missed many, but he never gave up.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L04-U3-LS2-1","dok":1,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["It was the final match of the school football cup.","Andalus School was playing against Al-Noor School, and the score was 1–1.","Only two minutes were left.","Omar, the team captain, wiped his face with the sleeve of his green jacket.","All year, he had scored more goals than anyone else on the team.","Everyone expected him to win the trophy for them.","Suddenly, a player from Al-Noor tripped Sami near the goal.","The referee blew his whistle.","\"Penalty!\" he shouted.","The crowd jumped to their feet.","Omar picked up the ball.","Then he looked at Sami.","Sami was sitting on the grass and rubbing his knee, but he was not badly hurt.","Omar remembered all the afternoons when Sami had stayed after practice.","While the others went home, Sami kicked penalty after penalty at the empty goal.","He missed many, but he never gave up.","Still, he had never scored in a real match.","\"Sami,\" Omar said, holding out the ball.","\"You take it.\"","Sami's eyes grew wide.","\"Me?","But you're our best player!\"","\"You've practiced this more than any of us,\" Omar said.","\"I believe in you.\"","Mr.","Khalid, the coach, watched from the side.","He nodded slowly.","Sami placed the ball on the spot.","His hands were shaking.","He took a deep breath, ran forward and kicked.","The goalkeeper dived to the left.","The ball flew to the right – into the net!","The crowd went wild.","When the final whistle blew, the players lifted Sami onto their shoulders.","Later, Mr.","Khalid shook Omar's hand.","\"A good player scores goals,\" he said.","\"A great captain helps others score them.\""]},{"q":"Underline the words that show Sami was nervous.","answer":"His hands were shaking.","explanation":"Body clue.","explanation_ar":"يداه ترتجفان.","evidence":"His hands were shaking.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L04-U3-LS2-1","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["It was the final match of the school football cup.","Andalus School was playing against Al-Noor School, and the score was 1–1.","Only two minutes were left.","Omar, the team captain, wiped his face with the sleeve of his green jacket.","All year, he had scored more goals than anyone else on the team.","Everyone expected him to win the trophy for them.","Suddenly, a player from Al-Noor tripped Sami near the goal.","The referee blew his whistle.","\"Penalty!\" he shouted.","The crowd jumped to their feet.","Omar picked up the ball.","Then he looked at Sami.","Sami was sitting on the grass and rubbing his knee, but he was not badly hurt.","Omar remembered all the afternoons when Sami had stayed after practice.","While the others went home, Sami kicked penalty after penalty at the empty goal.","He missed many, but he never gave up.","Still, he had never scored in a real match.","\"Sami,\" Omar said, holding out the ball.","\"You take it.\"","Sami's eyes grew wide.","\"Me?","But you're our best player!\"","\"You've practiced this more than any of us,\" Omar said.","\"I believe in you.\"","Mr.","Khalid, the coach, watched from the side.","He nodded slowly.","Sami placed the ball on the spot.","His hands were shaking.","He took a deep breath, ran forward and kicked.","The goalkeeper dived to the left.","The ball flew to the right – into the net!","The crowd went wild.","When the final whistle blew, the players lifted Sami onto their shoulders.","Later, Mr.","Khalid shook Omar's hand.","\"A good player scores goals,\" he said.","\"A great captain helps others score them.\""]},{"q":"Why did everyone EXPECT Omar to take the penalty?","answer":"He had scored more goals than anyone else all year.","explanation":"Paragraph 2.","explanation_ar":"لأنه الهدّاف.","options":["He was the tallest player.","He was the goalkeeper.","The coach had told him to.","He had scored more goals than anyone else all year."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Why does the writer tell us that Sami *had never scored in a real match*?","answer":"to show that Omar's choice was a big risk","explanation":"Author's craft.","explanation_ar":"ليُظهر أن القرار مخاطرة.","options":["to show that Omar's choice was a big risk","to make the story shorter","to show Sami was lazy","to explain the score"],"dok":3,"skill":"author's craft","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS2-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Explain and give your opinion.","instructions_ar":"اشرح وأبدِ رأيك.","items":[{"q":"Explain WHY Omar gave the penalty to Sami. Use two clues.","answer":"Omar remembered that Sami stayed after practice to kick penalties, and he said, 'You've practiced this more than any of us.'","explanation":"Two clues.","explanation_ar":"دليلان.","dok":2,"skill":"motivation","stage":"production"},{"q":"What happened because of Omar's choice?","answer":"Sami scored, the team won the cup, and Sami felt proud.","explanation":"Result.","explanation_ar":"النتيجة.","dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write the theme of the story in one sentence and give evidence.","answer":"A great leader helps others succeed. Evidence: 'A great captain helps others score them.'","explanation":"Theme + evidence.","explanation_ar":"المغزى + الدليل.","dok":3,"skill":"theme","stage":"production"},{"q":"Was it the right choice? What would you do? Why?","answer":"Yes, because Sami worked hard and deserved a chance, and the team still won.","explanation":"Opinion + reason.","explanation_ar":"رأي + سبب.","dok":3,"skill":"evaluate","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS2-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"The Captain's Choice\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “The Captain's Choice”.","answer":"272 words","title":"The Captain's Choice","body":"It was the final match of the school football cup. Andalus School was playing against Al-Noor School, and the score was 1–1. Only two minutes were left.\n\nOmar, the team captain, wiped his face with the sleeve of his green jacket. All year, he had scored more goals than anyone else on the team. Everyone expected him to win the trophy for them.\n\nSuddenly, a player from Al-Noor tripped Sami near the goal. The referee blew his whistle. \"Penalty!\" he shouted. The crowd jumped to their feet.\n\nOmar picked up the ball. Then he looked at Sami. Sami was sitting on the grass and rubbing his knee, but he was not badly hurt. Omar remembered all the afternoons when Sami had stayed after practice. While the others went home, Sami kicked penalty after penalty at the empty goal. He missed many, but he never gave up. Still, he had never scored in a real match.\n\n\"Sami,\" Omar said, holding out the ball. \"You take it.\"\n\nSami's eyes grew wide. \"Me? But you're our best player!\"\n\n\"You've practiced this more than any of us,\" Omar said. \"I believe in you.\"\n\nMr. Khalid, the coach, watched from the side. He nodded slowly.\n\nSami placed the ball on the spot. His hands were shaking. He took a deep breath, ran forward and kicked. The goalkeeper dived to the left. The ball flew to the right – into the net!\n\nThe crowd went wild. When the final whistle blew, the players lifted Sami onto their shoulders.\n\nLater, Mr. Khalid shook Omar's hand. \"A good player scores goals,\" he said. \"A great captain helps others score them.\"","words":272,"limit":207}],"time_limit_sec":207}],"game":{"name":"Choice Detective","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Detective board: the child drags quote cards into WORDS, ACTIONS or MEMORIES; each correct clue lights up a magnifying glass. With three clues, the child chooses the theme from four options to solve the case.","Teams get a pile of clue cards from the story.","They sort each clue into WORDS, ACTIONS or MEMORIES.","They explain how each clue shows WHY Omar chose Sami.","They write the theme on the theme card.","Each correct clue = 1 point; a correct theme with evidence = 3 points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Where does *The Captain's Choice* take place?","answer":"at a school football final","explanation":"Setting.","explanation_ar":"في نهائي كرة القدم المدرسي.","options":["at a swimming pool","in a classroom","at a basketball court","at a school football final"],"dok":1,"skill":"setting"},{"q":"Who watched from the side and nodded?","answer":"Mr. Khalid, the coach","explanation":"Paragraph 8.","explanation_ar":"المدرب خالد.","options":["the referee","Hamza","the goalkeeper","Mr. Khalid, the coach"],"dok":1,"skill":"characters"},{"q":"*The **crowd** jumped to their feet.* A *crowd* is ___.","answer":"a large group of people","explanation":"Crowd.","explanation_ar":"حشد.","options":["a football","a whistle","a large group of people","a goalkeeper"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Which sentence about Omar's choice is correct?","answer":"Omar gave the ball to Sami.","explanation":"gave.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Omar gave the ball to Sami.","Omar give the ball to Sami.","Omar gived the ball to Sami.","Omar given the ball to Sami."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"What does *The crowd went wild* mean?","answer":"The people became very excited.","explanation":"Idiom.","explanation_ar":"تحمّس الجمهور كثيرًا.","options":["The people ran into the desert.","The people were angry.","The people became very excited.","The people went home."],"dok":2,"skill":"figurative language"},{"q":"What is a character's *motivation*?","answer":"the reason inside him for doing something","explanation":"Motivation.","explanation_ar":"الدافع.","options":["the place of the story","the reason inside him for doing something","the last event","the title"],"dok":2,"skill":"motivation"},{"q":"Which is a THEME, not an event, in *The Captain's Choice*?","answer":"Helping others succeed is a sign of a great leader.","explanation":"Theme = lesson.","explanation_ar":"درس للحياة.","options":["Helping others succeed is a sign of a great leader.","Sami kicked the ball to the right.","The score was 1–1.","The referee blew his whistle."],"dok":2,"skill":"theme"},{"q":"How did Sami probably feel when Omar gave him the ball?","answer":"surprised and nervous","explanation":"'Me?' + hands shaking.","explanation_ar":"متفاجئًا ومتوترًا.","options":["bored","surprised and nervous","angry","sleepy"],"dok":2,"skill":"inference"},{"q":"What would the story LOSE without the memory of Sami practicing?","answer":"We would not understand why Omar chose him.","explanation":"Motivation clue.","explanation_ar":"لن نفهم سبب الاختيار.","options":["We would not understand why Omar chose him.","We would not know the score.","We would not know the setting.","Nothing at all."],"dok":3,"skill":"author's craft"},{"q":"Which saying matches the theme of the story?","answer":"Together, everyone achieves more.","explanation":"Teamwork.","explanation_ar":"معًا نحقق أكثر.","options":["The early bird catches the worm.","Don't judge a book by its cover.","Together, everyone achieves more.","Look before you leap."],"dok":3,"skill":"theme"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'final': two teams in a cup final"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'expect': fans looking at one player"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'referee': a referee with a whistle"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'penalty': a ball on the penalty spot"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'crowd': a stadium full of fans"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'dive': a goalkeeper diving"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'believe in': a captain smiling at a nervous teammate"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-01","prompt":"Omar holding out the ball to a surprised Sami."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-02","prompt":"Sami scoring a penalty as the goalkeeper dives the wrong way."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS2-03","prompt":"A chart for explaining a character's choice."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V01","script":"final. Our team played in the final."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V02","script":"expect. Everyone expected Omar to take the penalty."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V03","script":"referee. The referee blew his whistle."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V04","script":"penalty. Sami took the penalty."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V05","script":"crowd. The crowd went wild."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V06","script":"dive. The goalkeeper dived to the left."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-V07","script":"believe in. \"I believe in you,\" said Omar."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-T1","script":"It was the final match of the school football cup. Andalus School was playing against Al-Noor School, and the score was 1–1. Only two minutes were left. Omar, the team captain, wiped his face with the sleeve of his green jacket. All year, he had scored more goals than anyone else on the team. Everyone expected him to win the trophy for them. Suddenly, a player from Al-Noor tripped Sami near the goal. The referee blew his whistle. \"Penalty!\" he shouted. The crowd jumped to their feet. Omar picked up the ball. Then he looked at Sami. Sami was sitting on the grass and rubbing his knee, but he was not badly hurt. Omar remembered all the afternoons when Sami had stayed after practice. While the others went home, Sami kicked penalty after penalty at the empty goal. He missed many, but he never gave up. Still, he had never scored in a real match. \"Sami,\" Omar said, holding out the ball. \"You take it.\" Sami's eyes grew wide. \"Me? But you're our best player!\" \"You've practiced this more than any of us,\" Omar said. \"I believe in you.\" Mr. Khalid, the coach, watched from the side. He nodded slowly. Sami placed the ball on the spot. His hands were shaking. He took a deep breath, ran forward and kicked. The goalkeeper dived to the left. The ball flew to the right – into the net! The crowd went wild. When the final whistle blew, the players lifted Sami onto their shoulders. Later, Mr. Khalid shook Omar's hand. \"A good player scores goals,\" he said. \"A great captain helps others score them.\""},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS2-VID","script":"The final match. 1–1. Two minutes left. What would YOU do? It was the final match of the school football cup… What did Omar choose? Why? What happened? The theme is a lesson about life: A great captain helps others succeed. Who helps YOU succeed? Who can you help?"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS3","title":"Point of view: first and third person: \"Every School Needs a Sports Day\"","lesson_type":"strategy_paired_text","objectives":["identify first-person and third-person point of view in a story and an opinion text","explain how the point of view changes what the reader knows","rewrite sentences from third person to first person and compare the two texts"],"objectives_ar":["تحديد وجهة النظر بضمير المتكلم وضمير الغائب في قصة ونص رأي.","شرح كيف تغيّر وجهة النظر ما يعرفه القارئ.","إعادة كتابة جمل من ضمير الغائب إلى ضمير المتكلم ومقارنة النصين."],"success_criteria":["I can find the pronouns that show the point of view.","I can say who is telling the text and whose thoughts we know.","I can change a sentence from third person to first person."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع إيجاد الضمائر التي تُظهر وجهة النظر.","أستطيع قول من يروي النص وأفكار مَن نعرف.","أستطيع تحويل جملة من ضمير الغائب إلى ضمير المتكلم."],"map_area":"Informational Text: Language, Craft, and Structure","vocabulary":[{"word":"narrator","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈnærˌeɪtər/","definition":"the person or voice that tells a story","arabic":"الراوي","example":"The narrator tells us what Omar remembers.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"relay race","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈriˌleɪ reɪs/","definition":"a race where each team member runs one part","arabic":"سباق التتابع","example":"Our team came second in the relay race.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"include","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɪnˈklud/","definition":"to make someone part of a group","arabic":"يضمّ / يشمل","example":"A good game includes everyone.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"judge","pos":"noun","ipa":"/dʒʌdʒ/","definition":"a person who decides who wins","arabic":"حَكَم / مُحكّم","example":"Two teachers were judges at the race.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"scorekeeper","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈskɔrˌkipər/","definition":"a person who writes down the points","arabic":"مسجّل النقاط","example":"Adam was the scorekeeper.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"disagree","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌdɪsəˈɡri/","definition":"to have a different opinion","arabic":"يعارض / يختلف في الرأي","example":"Some people say sports day wastes time. I disagree.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"fair play","pos":"noun","ipa":"/fɛr pleɪ/","definition":"playing honestly and following the rules","arabic":"اللعب النظيف","example":"We learn fair play on sports day.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"The **point of view** tells us **who is telling** the text. Look at the **pronouns** to find it.\n\n**First person:** the narrator is **inside** the text and tells about **himself or herself**: **I, me, my, we, us, our**. We know the narrator's own thoughts and feelings. *Every School Needs a Sports Day* is in **first person** – Layla tells it.\n\n**Third person:** the narrator is **outside** the story and tells about **other people**: **he, she, they, him, her, their** and **names**. The narrator can tell us what the characters do and sometimes what they think. *The Captain's Choice* is in **third person**.","examples":["First person: ***I** believe that every school should have a sports day.* (Layla)","First person: *In the relay race last year, **my** team was last.* – Layla's own memory.","First person plural: ***We** cheered each other on, and **we** finished second!*","Third person: ***Omar** picked up the ball. Then **he** looked at Sami.*","Third person: *Omar remembered all the afternoons when Sami had stayed after practice.* – the narrator tells us what is in Omar's mind.","Change to first person (Omar): ***I** picked up the ball. Then **I** looked at Sami.*","Change to first person (Sami): ***My** hands were shaking. **I** took a deep breath.*","Careful! *\"I believe in you,\" Omar said.* has **I** inside quotation marks – it is dialogue, but the story is still **third person**.","Different perspective: from **Sami's** point of view, we could learn how scared he felt; from **Omar's**, why he chose Sami."],"common_errors":["✗ The story is first person because it has 'I'. → ✓ Check outside the quotation marks. (**I** in dialogue doesn't change the point of view.)","✗ Layla is third person because she talks about Adam. → ✓ It is first person: Layla says I and my. (Who is **telling**?)","✗ I picked up the ball. Then he looked at Sami. → ✓ I picked up the ball. Then I looked at Sami. (Keep **one** point of view.)","✗ Me and my team finished second. → ✓ My team and I finished second. (Use **I** as the subject; put others first.)","✗ Mixing up the narrator and the writer. → ✓ The narrator is the voice inside the text. (Narrator ≠ always the author.)","✗ Our team were second. → ✓ Our team was second. (One team → **was**.)"],"arabic":"وجهة النظر تخبرنا مَن يروي النص، وتُعرف من الضمائر.\n\nضمير المتكلم: الراوي داخل النص ويتحدث عن نفسه (I, me, my, we, our)، فنعرف أفكاره ومشاعره. نص ليلى بضمير المتكلم.\n\nضمير الغائب: الراوي خارج القصة ويتحدث عن الآخرين (he, she, they والأسماء). قصة «قرار القائد» بضمير الغائب.\n\nانتبه: كلمة I داخل علامات التنصيص حوار، ولا تغيّر وجهة نظر القصة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Who is telling the story? Let's find out with the pronoun detectives!","on_screen":"Point of View 👀","visual":"Layla and Sami hold magnifying glasses over the words I and he."},{"time":"00:20–01:20","narration":"I believe that every school should have a sports day…","on_screen":"(Layla's opinion text)","visual":"Sports day scenes: a relay race, Adam winning the wheelchair race, families cheering."},{"time":"01:20–02:00","narration":"I, me, my, we – first person. He, she, they, names – third person!","on_screen":"First person · Third person","visual":"Pronouns fly into two goals labelled 1st and 3rd."},{"time":"02:00–02:40","narration":"Omar picked up the ball. → I picked up the ball.","on_screen":"Change it! 🔄","visual":"The sentence changes as Omar turns to face the camera."},{"time":"02:40–03:00","narration":"Same match, different eyes – every person has a perspective!","on_screen":"perspective","visual":"The same penalty shown from Sami's eyes and from the crowd."}],"captions_ar":["مَن يروي القصة؟ لنكتشف ذلك مع محققي الضمائر!","أعتقد أن كل مدرسة يجب أن يكون فيها يوم رياضي…","I, me, my, we للمتكلم. he, she, they والأسماء للغائب!","التقط عمر الكرة ← التقطتُ الكرة.","المباراة نفسها بعيون مختلفة؛ لكل شخص وجهة نظر!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, friendly female teacher, speed 0.90. Layla reads her text; a storyteller voice reads the story lines."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Every School Needs a Sports Day (by Layla)","body":"I believe that every school should have a sports day. I have three strong reasons.\n\nFirst, a sports day keeps us healthy. Many children sit for hours at desks and in front of screens. On sports day, we run, jump and move all day long, and we learn that exercise can be fun.\n\nSecond, a sports day teaches teamwork. In the relay race last year, my team was last after the first runner. Nobody gave up. We cheered each other on, and we finished second! I learned that we are stronger together.\n\nThird, a sports day includes everyone. My friend Adam uses a wheelchair, and he won the wheelchair race. Students who don't like running can be judges or scorekeepers, or they can cheer for their classmates. Families come to watch, too.\n\nSome people say that a sports day wastes a day of learning. I disagree. On sports day, we learn about our bodies, respect and fair play.\n\nFor these reasons, I think every school needs a sports day. Let's make it happen!","word_count":173,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U3-LS3-1","genre":"opinion/argument","role":"paired","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[{"word":"relay race","definition":"a race where each runner in a team runs one part, then passes a stick to the next runner","arabic":"سباق التتابع"},{"word":"judge","definition":"a person who decides who wins","arabic":"حَكَم"},{"word":"fair play","definition":"playing honestly and following the rules","arabic":"اللعب النظيف"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read *Every School Needs a Sports Day*. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What is Layla's opinion about sports days?","answer":"Every school should have a sports day.","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"يجب أن يكون في كل مدرسة يوم رياضي.","options":["Sports days waste time.","Only boys should do sports.","Schools need longer lessons.","Every school should have a sports day."],"dok":1,"skill":"opinion","text_id":"TXT-RW-L04-U3-LS3-1","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What is Layla's FIRST reason for a school sports day?","answer":"A sports day keeps us healthy.","explanation":"First, …","explanation_ar":"يحافظ على صحتنا.","options":["Families come to watch.","Adam won a race.","A sports day keeps us healthy.","It is a holiday."],"dok":1,"skill":"reasons","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What happened to Layla's team in the relay race?","answer":"It was last at first, but it finished second.","explanation":"Paragraph 3.","explanation_ar":"كان أخيرًا ثم حلّ ثانيًا.","options":["It was last at first, but it finished second.","It won first place.","It gave up.","It did not run."],"dok":2,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which race did Adam win?","answer":"the wheelchair race","explanation":"Paragraph 4.","explanation_ar":"سباق الكراسي المتحركة.","options":["the relay race","the long jump","the football match","the wheelchair race"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What can students who don't like running do on sports day?","answer":"be judges or scorekeepers, or cheer for their classmates","explanation":"Paragraph 4.","explanation_ar":"يكونون حكامًا أو مسجلي نقاط أو يشجعون.","options":["stay at home","be judges or scorekeepers, or cheer for their classmates","sleep in class","only watch TV"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What do *some people* say about sports day?","answer":"It wastes a day of learning.","explanation":"Paragraph 5.","explanation_ar":"يضيّع يومًا من التعلّم.","options":["It is too short.","It wastes a day of learning.","It needs more trophies.","It should be every week."],"dok":2,"skill":"counterargument","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS3-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Point of view. Choose.","instructions_ar":"وجهة النظر: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which pronouns show that Layla's text is in FIRST person?","answer":"I, my, we, our","explanation":"First person.","explanation_ar":"I, my, we, our.","options":["he, she, they","him, her, them","I, my, we, our","it, its"],"dok":1,"skill":"point of view","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Who is the narrator of *The Captain's Choice*?","answer":"a voice outside the story","explanation":"Third person.","explanation_ar":"راوٍ خارج القصة.","options":["Omar","a voice outside the story","Sami","Mr. Khalid"],"dok":2,"skill":"point of view","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*\"I believe in you,\" Omar said.* Why is *The Captain's Choice* still THIRD person?","answer":"The word *I* is inside the dialogue, not in the narration.","explanation":"Dialogue ≠ narrator.","explanation_ar":"لأن I داخل الحوار.","options":["The word *I* is inside the dialogue, not in the narration.","Omar is the narrator.","The story has no pronouns.","It is a poem."],"dok":3,"skill":"point of view","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Change to first person (Omar): *Omar picked up the ball.*","answer":"I picked up the ball.","explanation":"Omar → I.","explanation_ar":"I picked up the ball.","options":["He picked up the ball.","They picked up the ball.","I picked up the ball.","Omar picks up me."],"dok":1,"skill":"rewriting","stage":"guided"},{"q":"In which text do we learn the narrator's OWN memories?","answer":"the opinion text, because Layla tells about her relay race","explanation":"First person.","explanation_ar":"نص الرأي.","options":["the opinion text, because Layla tells about her relay race","the story, because the narrator played in the match","neither text","both texts are told by Sami"],"dok":2,"skill":"point of view","stage":"guided"},{"q":"If Sami told the penalty in first person, which sentence would he write?","answer":"My hands were shaking, but I ran forward and kicked.","explanation":"Sami → I / my.","explanation_ar":"بضمير المتكلم.","options":["His hands were shaking, but he ran forward.","Sami's hands were shaking.","Their hands were shaking.","My hands were shaking, but I ran forward and kicked."],"dok":3,"skill":"perspective","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS3-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Complete the Point of View Chart for both texts.","instructions_ar":"أكمل جدول وجهة النظر للنصين.","items":[{"q":"Row 1 – Who is telling each text?","answer":"The story is told by a narrator outside the story. The opinion text is told by Layla.","explanation":"Narrator.","explanation_ar":"الراوي.","dok":1,"skill":"point of view","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Row 2 – Which pronouns does each text use?","answer":"Story: he, they, Omar, Sami. Opinion: I, my, we, our.","explanation":"Pronouns.","explanation_ar":"الضمائر.","dok":1,"skill":"point of view","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Row 3 – Whose thoughts and feelings do we learn?","answer":"In the story, we learn mostly what Omar remembers and believes. In the opinion text, we learn Layla's own ideas and memories.","explanation":"Thoughts.","explanation_ar":"الأفكار.","dok":2,"skill":"point of view","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Row 4 – Copy one example sentence from each text.","answer":"'Then he looked at Sami.' / 'I believe that every school should have a sports day.'","explanation":"Evidence.","explanation_ar":"الدليل.","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS3-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Rewrite and compare.","instructions_ar":"أعد الكتابة وقارن.","items":[{"q":"Rewrite in first person as Sami: *Sami placed the ball on the spot. His hands were shaking.*","answer":"I placed the ball on the spot. My hands were shaking.","explanation":"I / my.","explanation_ar":"I / my.","dok":2,"skill":"rewriting","stage":"production"},{"q":"Rewrite in third person about Layla: *I learned that we are stronger together.*","answer":"Layla learned that her team was stronger together.","explanation":"she / her / names.","explanation_ar":"she / her.","dok":2,"skill":"rewriting","stage":"production"},{"q":"How would the penalty be different if Sami told it? What could we learn?","answer":"We could learn how scared and happy Sami felt and what he was thinking before he kicked.","explanation":"Perspective.","explanation_ar":"منظور.","dok":3,"skill":"perspective","stage":"production"},{"q":"How are the two texts alike in their message?","answer":"Both show that teamwork, effort and including everyone make sports special.","explanation":"Compare.","explanation_ar":"قارن.","dok":3,"skill":"compare texts","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS3-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"Every School Needs a Sports Day (by Layla)\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “Every School Needs a Sports Day (by Layla)”.","answer":"173 words","title":"Every School Needs a Sports Day (by Layla)","body":"I believe that every school should have a sports day. I have three strong reasons.\n\nFirst, a sports day keeps us healthy. Many children sit for hours at desks and in front of screens. On sports day, we run, jump and move all day long, and we learn that exercise can be fun.\n\nSecond, a sports day teaches teamwork. In the relay race last year, my team was last after the first runner. Nobody gave up. We cheered each other on, and we finished second! I learned that we are stronger together.\n\nThird, a sports day includes everyone. My friend Adam uses a wheelchair, and he won the wheelchair race. Students who don't like running can be judges or scorekeepers, or they can cheer for their classmates. Families come to watch, too.\n\nSome people say that a sports day wastes a day of learning. I disagree. On sports day, we learn about our bodies, respect and fair play.\n\nFor these reasons, I think every school needs a sports day. Let's make it happen!","words":173,"limit":137}],"time_limit_sec":137},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS3-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Point of View Chart","instructions":"Organizer: Fill in each row for both texts: The Captain's Choice (story) and Every School Needs a Sports Day (opinion).","items":[{"q":"Who is telling the text?","answer":"Story: a narrator outside the story · Opinion: Layla herself"},{"q":"Which pronouns are used?","answer":"Story: he, they, Omar, Sami (third person) · Opinion: I, my, we, our (first person)"},{"q":"Whose thoughts and feelings do we learn?","answer":"Story: mostly Omar's (what he remembers and believes) · Opinion: Layla's own opinions and memories"},{"q":"Example sentence as evidence","answer":"Story: 'Then he looked at Sami.' · Opinion: 'I believe that every school should have a sports day.'"}]}],"game":{"name":"Pronoun Goalkeeper","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Goalkeeper: sentences fly toward two goals; the child taps 1st or 3rd before the ball arrives. Correct taps are saved by Saqr the goalkeeper; extra levels ask the child to rewrite the sentence in the other point of view.","The teacher reads a sentence card.","The player shouts '1st!' or '3rd!' and names the pronoun that proves it.","A correct answer lets the player throw the ball at that goal for a point.","Bonus: change the sentence to the other point of view for 2 points.","The team with the most points wins."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Which word shows FIRST-person point of view?","answer":"my","explanation":"First person.","explanation_ar":"my.","options":["his","my","their","she"],"dok":1,"skill":"point of view"},{"q":"*Then he looked at Sami.* This sentence is in ___.","answer":"third person","explanation":"he.","explanation_ar":"ضمير الغائب.","options":["first person","a poem","third person","a question"],"dok":1,"skill":"point of view"},{"q":"A *narrator* is ___.","answer":"the voice that tells the story","explanation":"Narrator.","explanation_ar":"الراوي.","options":["the voice that tells the story","the winner of the race","the coach","a kind of ball"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*Some people say sports day wastes time. I **disagree**.* *Disagree* means ___.","answer":"have a different opinion","explanation":"Disagree.","explanation_ar":"أعارض.","options":["agree completely","fall asleep","have a different opinion","run a race"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Which sentence about Layla's relay team is correct?","answer":"My team and I finished second.","explanation":"My team and I.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Me and my team finished second.","My team and I finished second.","My team and me finished second.","I and my team finishes second."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Change to first person (Layla): *Layla's team was last.*","answer":"My team was last.","explanation":"Layla → my.","explanation_ar":"My team was last.","options":["Her team was last.","Their team was last.","Layla's team were last.","My team was last."],"dok":2,"skill":"rewriting"},{"q":"Why does Layla tell us about her own relay race?","answer":"to support her reason with a personal example","explanation":"Example as evidence.","explanation_ar":"لتدعم السبب بمثال شخصي.","options":["to tell a story with no point","to support her reason with a personal example","to show she is the fastest","to make the text shorter"],"dok":2,"skill":"author's purpose"},{"q":"In which point of view can a narrator tell us what SEVERAL characters do from outside the story?","answer":"third person","explanation":"Third person.","explanation_ar":"ضمير الغائب.","options":["third person","first person","no point of view","second person only"],"dok":2,"skill":"point of view"},{"q":"How does the point of view of *The Captain's Choice* help the reader?","answer":"We can see what Omar remembers and also what the others do.","explanation":"Third person.","explanation_ar":"نرى ذكريات عمر وأفعال الآخرين.","options":["We only know Sami's thoughts.","We cannot know anything about Omar.","It makes the story a poem.","We can see what Omar remembers and also what the others do."],"dok":3,"skill":"point of view"},{"q":"What do BOTH texts show about sports?","answer":"Teamwork and effort matter more than winning alone.","explanation":"Compare.","explanation_ar":"العمل الجماعي والجهد.","options":["Only the best players should play.","Sports days waste time.","Trophies are the most important thing.","Teamwork and effort matter more than winning alone."],"dok":3,"skill":"compare texts"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'narrator': a storyteller reading to children"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'relay race': runners passing a baton"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'include': a circle of children with one more joining"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'judge': a judge holding a clipboard at a finish line"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'scorekeeper': a child writing scores on a board"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'disagree': two children with different thought bubbles"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'fair play': players helping an opponent up"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-01","prompt":"A school sports day with a relay race and a wheelchair race."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-02","prompt":"First-person and third-person pronouns."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS3-03","prompt":"A point of view chart for two texts."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V01","script":"narrator. The narrator tells us what Omar remembers."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V02","script":"relay race. Our team came second in the relay race."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V03","script":"include. A good game includes everyone."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V04","script":"judge. Two teachers were judges at the race."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V05","script":"scorekeeper. Adam was the scorekeeper."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V06","script":"disagree. Some people say sports day wastes time. I disagree."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-V07","script":"fair play. We learn fair play on sports day."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-T1","script":"I believe that every school should have a sports day. I have three strong reasons. First, a sports day keeps us healthy. Many children sit for hours at desks and in front of screens. On sports day, we run, jump and move all day long, and we learn that exercise can be fun. Second, a sports day teaches teamwork. In the relay race last year, my team was last after the first runner. Nobody gave up. We cheered each other on, and we finished second! I learned that we are stronger together. Third, a sports day includes everyone. My friend Adam uses a wheelchair, and he won the wheelchair race. Students who don't like running can be judges or scorekeepers, or they can cheer for their classmates. Families come to watch, too. Some people say that a sports day wastes a day of learning. I disagree. On sports day, we learn about our bodies, respect and fair play. For these reasons, I think every school needs a sports day. Let's make it happen!"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS3-VID","script":"Who is telling the story? Let's find out with the pronoun detectives! I believe that every school should have a sports day… I, me, my, we – first person. He, she, they, names – third person! Omar picked up the ball. → I picked up the ball. Same match, different eyes – every person has a perspective!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS4","title":"Writing Skill: Dialogue punctuation","lesson_type":"writing_skill","objectives":["punctuate dialogue correctly with quotation marks, commas and end marks","use speaker tags (said, asked, shouted, whispered) before, after and in the middle of a quote","start a new paragraph for each new speaker"],"objectives_ar":["ترقيم الحوار بشكل صحيح بعلامات التنصيص والفواصل وعلامات النهاية.","استخدام عبارات المتحدث قبل الاقتباس وبعده وفي وسطه.","بدء فقرة جديدة لكل متحدث جديد."],"success_criteria":["I can put quotation marks around a speaker's exact words.","I can put commas and end marks inside the quotation marks.","I can start a new line for a new speaker and use strong speaker tags."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع وضع علامات التنصيص حول كلمات المتحدث بالضبط.","أستطيع وضع الفواصل وعلامات النهاية داخل علامات التنصيص.","أستطيع بدء سطر جديد لمتحدث جديد واستخدام أفعال قول قوية."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"dialogue","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdaɪəˌlɔɡ/","definition":"the words that characters say to each other","arabic":"حوار","example":"Noura's story has a lot of dialogue.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"quotation marks","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kwoʊˈteɪʃən mɑrks/","definition":"the marks \" \" that go around the exact words someone says","arabic":"علامات التنصيص","example":"Put quotation marks around the words people say.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"speaker tag","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈspikər tæɡ/","definition":"the words that tell who is speaking, like 'she said'","arabic":"عبارة المتحدث","example":"'Layla shouted' is a speaker tag.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"baton","pos":"noun","ipa":"/bəˈtɑn/","definition":"a short stick that runners pass in a relay race","arabic":"عصا التتابع","example":"Layla passed me the baton.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"jelly","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdʒɛli/","definition":"a soft, sweet food that shakes","arabic":"جيلي (هلام)","example":"My legs felt like jelly.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"agree","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əˈɡri/","definition":"to have the same opinion","arabic":"يوافق","example":"\"Yes,\" Mr. Khalid agreed.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"proudly","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈpraʊdli/","definition":"in a way that shows you feel good about what you did","arabic":"بفخر","example":"\"I did it!\" Noura said proudly.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"**Dialogue** shows the exact words characters say. Put **quotation marks** around **only the spoken words**. Use a **speaker tag** (said, asked, shouted, whispered) to show **who** speaks and **how**.\n\n**Rule 1 – Tag after:** *\"We can win,\" Omar said.* → comma **inside** the quotes, then the tag. **Rule 2 – Tag before:** *Omar said, \"We can win.\"* → comma after the tag, capital letter, period **inside**. **Rule 3 – Questions and exclamations:** *\"Can I join in?\" Adam asked.* / *\"Goal!\" the fans shouted.* – no extra comma.\n\n**Rule 4 – Split quote:** *\"Yes,\" the coach said, \"you can play.\"* (one sentence: small letter) / *\"Yes,\" the coach said. \"You can play.\"* (two sentences: capital letter). **Rule 5 – New speaker, new paragraph.**","examples":["*\"I can't do it,\" I whispered.* (tag after; comma inside)","*He smiled and said, \"Just run your best.\"* (tag before; comma + capital letter)","*\"Go, Noura, go!\" everyone cheered.* (exclamation point inside; small letter for *everyone*)","*\"What did you learn today?\" Mr. Khalid asked.* (question mark inside)","*\"Yes,\" Mr. Khalid agreed. \"What did you learn today?\"* (split quote, two sentences)","*\"Pass the ball,\" shouted the captain, \"and run to the goal!\"* (split quote, one sentence)","Strong tags instead of *said*: **shouted, whispered, cheered, laughed, answered, agreed, called**.","Add how: *\"I learned never to give up,\" I answered **proudly**.*","Not dialogue: *Mr. Khalid told me to run my best.* (reported words – no quotation marks)"],"common_errors":["✗ \"We won\", Sami said. → ✓ \"We won,\" Sami said. (The comma goes **inside** the quotes.)","✗ Omar said \"pass the ball.\" → ✓ Omar said, \"Pass the ball.\" (Comma after the tag + **capital** letter.)","✗ \"Can I play?\", Adam asked. → ✓ \"Can I play?\" Adam asked. (No comma after **?** or **!**.)","✗ \"Goal!\" The fans shouted. → ✓ \"Goal!\" the fans shouted. (The tag continues the sentence: small letter.)","✗ Layla said that \"we were great.\" → ✓ Layla said that we were great. (No quotes for **reported** speech.)","✗ Two speakers in the same paragraph. → ✓ Start a new paragraph for each new speaker. (New speaker = new line.)","✗ \"I am tired\" said Noura. → ✓ \"I am tired,\" said Noura. (Don't forget the comma.)"],"arabic":"الحوار يُظهر كلمات الشخصيات بالضبط؛ ضع علامات التنصيص حول الكلام المنطوق فقط، واستخدم عبارة المتحدث لبيان من يتكلم وكيف.\n\nإذا جاءت عبارة المتحدث بعد الكلام: فاصلة داخل علامات التنصيص. وإذا جاءت قبله: فاصلة بعد العبارة وحرف كبير في بداية الكلام.\n\nعلامة الاستفهام والتعجب داخل علامات التنصيص، ولا نضيف بعدهما فاصلة.\n\nكل متحدث جديد يبدأ في سطر (فقرة) جديد، والكلام المنقول بصيغة غير مباشرة لا يحتاج علامات تنصيص."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Characters talk! How do we write what they say? Let's ask Noura.","on_screen":"Punctuating Dialogue 💬","visual":"Noura holds a giant pair of quotation marks like two goalposts."},{"time":"00:20–01:15","narration":"On sports day, our relay team was in last place…","on_screen":"(Noura's story)","visual":"The relay race animated; each spoken line appears in a speech bubble, then turns into a sentence with quotation marks."},{"time":"01:15–02:00","narration":"The quotation marks are the goal. Kick the comma and the end mark INSIDE the goal!","on_screen":"\" , \" · \" ? \" · \" ! \"","visual":"Punctuation marks fly into a goal shaped like quotation marks."},{"time":"02:00–02:40","narration":"Tag first? Comma, then a capital letter. New speaker? New line!","on_screen":"He said, \"Run!\"","visual":"The tag slides in front; a new line appears for each new speaker."},{"time":"02:40–03:00","narration":"Use strong tags: whispered, shouted, cheered, agreed!","on_screen":"said → shouted 📣","visual":"The word 'said' changes into stronger verbs."}],"captions_ar":["الشخصيات تتكلم! كيف نكتب ما تقوله؟ لنسأل نورة.","في اليوم الرياضي كان فريقنا للتتابع في المركز الأخير…","علامات التنصيص هي المرمى؛ أدخل الفاصلة وعلامة النهاية داخل المرمى!","عبارة المتحدث أولًا؟ فاصلة ثم حرف كبير. متحدث جديد؟ سطر جديد!","استخدم أفعالًا قوية: همس، صاح، هتف، وافق!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, lively female teacher, speed 0.90. Noura reads her story with different voices."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"The Last Runner (by Noura)","body":"On sports day, our relay team was in last place. I was the last runner, and my legs felt like jelly.\n\n\"I can't do it,\" I whispered to Mr. Khalid.\n\nHe smiled and said, \"Just run your best. That's all we need.\"\n\nWhen Layla passed me the baton, I ran as fast as I could. The crowd was shouting, and my baby sister Dana was waving from Mother's arms.\n\n\"Go, Noura, go!\" everyone cheered.\n\nI passed one runner, then another. Did I win? No, but our team finished second!\n\n\"You were amazing!\" Layla shouted as she hugged me.\n\n\"Yes,\" Mr. Khalid agreed. \"What did you learn today?\"\n\n\"I learned never to give up,\" I answered proudly.","word_count":116,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U3-LS4-1","genre":"model text","role":"model","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[],"annotations":["**Quotation marks** (\" \") go around the **exact words** a person says: *\"I can't do it,\" I whispered.*","**Punctuation inside:** the comma, period, question mark or exclamation point goes **inside** the closing quotation marks: *\"Go, Noura, go!\" everyone cheered.*","**Speaker first:** put a **comma** after the speaker tag and a **capital letter** at the start of the quote: *He smiled and said, \"Just run your best.\"*","**Split quote:** *\"Yes,\" Mr. Khalid agreed. \"What did you learn today?\"* – a new sentence inside the quote starts with a capital letter.","**New speaker = new paragraph.** Each time a different person speaks, start a new line.","**Strong speaker tags:** whispered, shouted, cheered, agreed, answered – they show **how** people speak. Add **-ly** words like *proudly*."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Noura's story. Choose the best answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ قصة نورة واختر أفضل إجابة.","items":[{"q":"Which runner was Noura in the relay?","answer":"the last runner","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"العدّاءة الأخيرة.","options":["the first runner","the second runner","the last runner","she did not run"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How did Noura's legs feel before her turn?","answer":"like jelly","explanation":"Paragraph 1.","explanation_ar":"كالجيلي.","options":["like rocks","like jelly","strong and fast","cold"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Who passed Noura the baton?","answer":"Layla","explanation":"Paragraph 4.","explanation_ar":"ليلى.","options":["Mr. Khalid","Dana","Sami","Layla"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What place did the team finish in?","answer":"second","explanation":"Paragraph 6.","explanation_ar":"الثاني.","options":["second","first","last","third"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did Noura learn?","answer":"never to give up","explanation":"Last line.","explanation_ar":"ألّا تستسلم أبدًا.","options":["never to give up","to run backward","to win every race","to stop when she is tired"],"dok":2,"skill":"theme","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How is Noura's story connected to Layla's opinion text?","answer":"It tells the same relay race from Noura's point of view.","explanation":"Same event, new perspective.","explanation_ar":"السباق نفسه من منظور نورة.","options":["It is about a football match.","It is told by Mr. Khalid.","It tells the same relay race from Noura's point of view.","It has no dialogue."],"dok":3,"skill":"compare texts","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS4-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Punctuating dialogue. Choose.","instructions_ar":"ترقيم الحوار: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which line from the relay race is punctuated correctly?","answer":"\"We can win,\" Layla said.","explanation":"Comma inside.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["\"We can win\", Layla said.","\"We can win,\" Layla said.","\"We can win.\" Layla said.","We can win, \"Layla said.\""],"dok":1,"skill":"dialogue punctuation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence with the coach's tag FIRST is correct?","answer":"The coach said, \"Warm up now.\"","explanation":"Comma + capital + period inside.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["The coach said \"warm up now.\"","The coach said, \"warm up now\".","The coach said. \"Warm up now.\"","The coach said, \"Warm up now.\""],"dok":2,"skill":"dialogue punctuation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which question from Adam is punctuated correctly?","answer":"\"Can I join in?\" Adam asked.","explanation":"? inside, no comma.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["\"Can I join in?\", Adam asked.","\"Can I join in\"? Adam asked.","\"Can I join in?\" Adam asked.","\"Can I join in.\" Adam asked?"],"dok":2,"skill":"dialogue punctuation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which shout from the fans is correct?","answer":"\"Goal!\" the fans shouted.","explanation":"Small letter after the quote.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["\"Goal!\" the fans shouted.","\"Goal!\" The fans shouted.","\"Goal\"! the fans shouted.","\"Goal!,\" the fans shouted."],"dok":2,"skill":"dialogue punctuation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"When must you start a new paragraph in dialogue?","answer":"when a different person starts speaking","explanation":"New speaker.","explanation_ar":"عند تغيّر المتحدث.","options":["after every three words","when a different person starts speaking","only at the end of the story","when the same person keeps talking"],"dok":1,"skill":"paragraphing","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence about Mr. Khalid's advice needs NO quotation marks?","answer":"Mr. Khalid told Noura to run her best.","explanation":"Reported speech.","explanation_ar":"كلام منقول.","options":["Mr. Khalid said, Run your best.","Run your best, Mr. Khalid said.","Mr. Khalid said, Just run.","Mr. Khalid told Noura to run her best."],"dok":3,"skill":"reported speech","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS4-A3","type":"sequence","stage":"freer","instructions":"Put in order: Build the dialogue lines.","instructions_ar":"ابنِ أسطر الحوار.","items":[{"q":"Build Omar's shout to Sami on the football field.","answer":"\"Pass the ball,\" → Omar → shouted → to Sami.","explanation":"Quote + comma inside + tag.","explanation_ar":"اقتباس + فاصلة + المتحدث.","stage":"freer","parts":["shouted","Omar","\"Pass the ball,\"","to Sami."],"target":["\"Pass the ball,\"","Omar","shouted","to Sami."]},{"q":"Build Hamza's question at the relay race.","answer":"Hamza asked, \"Is it my turn to run?\"","explanation":"Tag + comma + capital + ? inside.","explanation_ar":"المتحدث + فاصلة + ؟ داخل.","stage":"freer","parts":["Hamza","my turn","\"Is it","to run?\"","asked,"],"target":["Hamza","asked,","\"Is it","my turn","to run?\""]},{"q":"Build the referee's call at the end of the race.","answer":"\"Well done!\" the referee called loudly.","explanation":"! inside + small letter.","explanation_ar":"! داخل + حرف صغير.","stage":"freer","parts":["loudly.","called","\"Well done!\"","the referee"],"target":["\"Well done!\"","the referee","called","loudly."]},{"q":"Build Layla's split quote about her relay team.","answer":"\"Yes,\" Layla agreed. \"We never gave up.\"","explanation":"Split quote, two sentences.","explanation_ar":"اقتباس مقسوم.","stage":"freer","parts":["\"Yes,\"","\"We","Layla agreed.","gave up.\"","never"],"target":["\"Yes,\"","Layla agreed.","\"We","never","gave up.\""]}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS4-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write and fix dialogue.","instructions_ar":"اكتب الحوار وصحّحه.","items":[{"q":"Fix the punctuation: *we are a great team said the captain*","answer":"\"We are a great team,\" said the captain.","explanation":"Quotes + comma + capital.","explanation_ar":"تنصيص + فاصلة + حرف كبير.","dok":1,"skill":"editing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Fix the punctuation: *Sami asked can I take the penalty*","answer":"Sami asked, \"Can I take the penalty?\"","explanation":"Tag first.","explanation_ar":"المتحدث أولًا.","dok":2,"skill":"editing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write two lines of dialogue between two players. Start a new line for the second speaker.","answer":"\"I'm so tired,\" Faris said. (new line) \"Don't give up! We're almost there,\" Omar answered.","explanation":"Two speakers.","explanation_ar":"متحدثان.","dok":2,"skill":"writing dialogue","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a line of dialogue with a strong speaker tag and an -ly word.","answer":"\"We won the trophy!\" Sami shouted happily.","explanation":"Strong tag + -ly.","explanation_ar":"فعل قوي + -ly.","dok":2,"skill":"word choice","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Punctuation Penalty Kicks","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Penalty kicks: a dialogue line appears with flashing gaps; the child drags quotation marks, commas and end marks into the right gaps before the timer ends. A correct line scores; a wrong mark hits the post.","Teams take turns picking a dialogue strip.","They place punctuation cards in the gaps.","The other team checks with the rule card.","A correct strip = a penalty kick at the paper goal.","The team with the most goals wins."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What do quotation marks show?","answer":"the exact words someone says","explanation":"Quotes.","explanation_ar":"الكلام المنطوق بالضبط.","options":["the title of a book","the exact words someone says","a list of things","the end of a paragraph"],"dok":1,"skill":"dialogue punctuation"},{"q":"Where does the comma go in *\"We won\" Sami said*?","answer":"inside the quotation marks, after *won*","explanation":"Inside.","explanation_ar":"داخل التنصيص.","options":["inside the quotation marks, after *won*","after *Sami*","before *We*","after *said*"],"dok":1,"skill":"dialogue punctuation"},{"q":"Which word is a speaker tag?","answer":"whispered","explanation":"Tag.","explanation_ar":"whispered.","options":["whispered","baton","quickly","relay"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*\"Yes,\" Mr. Khalid **agreed**.* *Agreed* means ___.","answer":"had the same opinion","explanation":"Agree.","explanation_ar":"وافق.","options":["ran fast","felt sad","asked a question","had the same opinion"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Which sentence about the captain is punctuated correctly?","answer":"The captain said, \"Let's warm up.\"","explanation":"Comma + capital + period inside.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["The captain said \"let's warm up.\"","The captain said, \"let's warm up\".","The captain said, \"Let's warm up.\"","The captain, said \"Let's warm up.\""],"dok":2,"skill":"dialogue punctuation"},{"q":"Which question from Hamza is punctuated correctly?","answer":"\"Who scored the goal?\" Hamza asked.","explanation":"? inside.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["\"Who scored the goal\"? Hamza asked.","\"Who scored the goal?\", Hamza asked.","\"Who scored the goal?\" Hamza asked.","\"Who scored the goal.\" Hamza asked?"],"dok":2,"skill":"dialogue punctuation"},{"q":"Noura says a line, then Layla answers. What should the writer do?","answer":"Start a new paragraph for Layla.","explanation":"New speaker.","explanation_ar":"فقرة جديدة لليلى.","options":["Put both lines in one sentence.","Start a new paragraph for Layla.","Leave out Layla's words.","Use no quotation marks."],"dok":2,"skill":"paragraphing"},{"q":"Which split quote from the coach is correct?","answer":"\"Run fast,\" the coach said, \"and don't look back.\"","explanation":"One sentence split.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["\"Run fast,\" the coach said, \"and don't look back.\"","\"Run fast\" the coach said \"and don't look back.\"","\"Run fast,\" the coach said, \"And don't look back\".","\"Run fast, the coach said, and don't look back.\""],"dok":3,"skill":"dialogue punctuation"},{"q":"Which speaker tag shows that Noura was nervous?","answer":"\"I can't do it,\" I whispered.","explanation":"Word choice.","explanation_ar":"whispered.","options":["\"I can't do it,\" I shouted.","\"I can't do it,\" I cheered.","\"I can't do it,\" I laughed.","\"I can't do it,\" I whispered."],"dok":3,"skill":"word choice"},{"q":"Why do writers use dialogue in stories?","answer":"to show what characters think and feel through their own words","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"لإظهار أفكار الشخصيات ومشاعرها.","options":["to make the story shorter","to list facts","to show the date","to show what characters think and feel through their own words"],"dok":2,"skill":"author's craft"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'dialogue': two speech bubbles"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'quotation marks': large quotation marks"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'speaker tag': a label pointing to a speech bubble"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'baton': a hand passing a baton to another hand"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'jelly': a wobbly jelly on a plate"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'agree': two people nodding"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'proudly': a girl smiling with a medal"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-01","prompt":"Noura running the last part of a relay race."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-02","prompt":"A speech bubble changing into a sentence with quotation marks."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS4-03","prompt":"Punctuation marks going into a quotation-mark goal."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V01","script":"dialogue. Noura's story has a lot of dialogue."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V02","script":"quotation marks. Put quotation marks around the words people say."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V03","script":"speaker tag. 'Layla shouted' is a speaker tag."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V04","script":"baton. Layla passed me the baton."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V05","script":"jelly. My legs felt like jelly."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V06","script":"agree. \"Yes,\" Mr. Khalid agreed."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-V07","script":"proudly. \"I did it!\" Noura said proudly."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-T1","script":"On sports day, our relay team was in last place. I was the last runner, and my legs felt like jelly. \"I can't do it,\" I whispered to Mr. Khalid. He smiled and said, \"Just run your best. That's all we need.\" When Layla passed me the baton, I ran as fast as I could. The crowd was shouting, and my baby sister Dana was waving from Mother's arms. \"Go, Noura, go!\" everyone cheered. I passed one runner, then another. Did I win? No, but our team finished second! \"You were amazing!\" Layla shouted as she hugged me. \"Yes,\" Mr. Khalid agreed. \"What did you learn today?\" \"I learned never to give up,\" I answered proudly."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS4-VID","script":"Characters talk! How do we write what they say? Let's ask Noura. On sports day, our relay team was in last place… The quotation marks are the goal. Kick the comma and the end mark INSIDE the goal! Tag first? Comma, then a capital letter. New speaker? New line! Use strong tags: whispered, shouted, cheered, agreed!"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS5","title":"Writing Workshop: A Match to Remember","lesson_type":"writing_workshop","objectives":["plan a sports story with a Story Map (setting, characters, problem, events, ending)","write a story paragraph of 8–10 sentences in first person with at least three lines of correctly punctuated dialogue","revise, edit and publish 'A Match to Remember' in a class sports storybook"],"objectives_ar":["التخطيط لقصة رياضية بخريطة القصة (المكان، الشخصيات، المشكلة، الأحداث، النهاية).","كتابة فقرة قصصية من 8–10 جمل بضمير المتكلم فيها ثلاثة أسطر حوار على الأقل بترقيم صحيح.","تحسين القصة وتدقيقها ونشرها في كتاب قصص رياضية للصف."],"success_criteria":["I can write a beginning that tells the setting, the characters and the problem.","I can use dialogue with correct punctuation and a new line for each speaker.","I can write an ending that solves the problem and shows what I learned."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع كتابة بداية تذكر المكان والشخصيات والمشكلة.","أستطيع استخدام الحوار بترقيم صحيح وسطر جديد لكل متحدث.","أستطيع كتابة نهاية تحل المشكلة وتُظهر ما تعلّمته."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"setting","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsɛtɪŋ/","definition":"where and when a story happens","arabic":"المكان والزمان (في القصة)","example":"The setting is the sports hall.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"comeback","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkʌmˌbæk/","definition":"when a losing team starts to win again","arabic":"عودة (في المباراة)","example":"Our team made a big comeback.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"goggles","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡɑɡəlz/","definition":"special glasses that protect your eyes in water","arabic":"نظارات السباحة","example":"My goggles broke before the race.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"argue","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈɑrɡju/","definition":"to speak angrily because you disagree","arabic":"يتجادل","example":"The players started to argue.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"buzzer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbʌzər/","definition":"a machine that makes a loud sound to end a game","arabic":"صفّارة النهاية الآلية","example":"He scored just before the buzzer.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"calmly","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈkɑmli/","definition":"in a quiet, relaxed way","arabic":"بهدوء","example":"The coach spoke calmly.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"unforgettable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌʌnfərˈɡɛtəbəl/","definition":"so special that you will always remember it","arabic":"لا يُنسى","example":"It was an unforgettable match.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"A good story has a **beginning** (setting, characters, problem), a **middle** (events that build up to the most exciting moment) and an **end** (how the problem is solved and what the character learned).\n\nWrite in **first person** (I, we, my), so the reader feels they are in the match with you. Use **dialogue** to show feelings: *\"It's no use,\" he said.* is stronger than *He was sad.*\n\nUse **time transitions** (At half time, In the second half, With ten seconds left, Finally) and remember: **new speaker = new paragraph**, and punctuation goes **inside** the quotation marks.","examples":["Beginning (setting + problem): ***At half time, our basketball team was losing 20–10, and the sports hall felt very hot.***","Character + feeling with dialogue: ***\"It's no use,\" Faisal said. \"They're too fast for us.\"***","Turning point: ***Coach Saad looked at each of us. \"Stop trying to win alone and start passing,\" he said calmly.***","Middle event with a transition: ***In the second half, we listened.***","Building excitement: ***With ten seconds left, the score was 30–30.***","The exciting moment: ***\"Take the shot!\" Faisal shouted, but I saw that Badr was free under the basket.***","Solution: ***I threw him the ball, and he scored just before the buzzer.***","Ending + lesson: ***I will never forget that match because I learned that a team is stronger than any one player.***","Weak ending: *Then I went home. The end.* (no feeling, no lesson)"],"common_errors":["✗ Starting with the ending. → ✓ Start with the setting and the problem. (Beginning → middle → end.)","✗ Only dialogue, no action. → ✓ Mix dialogue with what characters do. (Balance talk and action.)","✗ \"Pass the ball\" I said. → ✓ \"Pass the ball,\" I said. (Comma inside the quotes.)","✗ Two speakers on one line. → ✓ New speaker = new line. (Paragraph rule.)","✗ Switching from I to he. → ✓ Keep first person: I, we, my. (One point of view.)","✗ Then… then… then… → ✓ At half time, In the second half, Finally (Vary your transitions.)","✗ Then I went home. The end. → ✓ I will never forget that match because… (End with a feeling or a lesson.)"],"arabic":"للقصة الجيدة بداية (المكان والشخصيات والمشكلة) ووسط (أحداث تتصاعد حتى اللحظة الأكثر إثارة) ونهاية (حل المشكلة وما تعلّمته الشخصية).\n\nاكتب بضمير المتكلم ليشعر القارئ أنه معك في المباراة، واستخدم الحوار لإظهار المشاعر.\n\nاستخدم كلمات الانتقال الزمنية، وتذكّر: متحدث جديد = سطر جديد، والترقيم داخل علامات التنصيص.\n\nاختم بشعور أو درس، لا بجملة مثل: ثم ذهبت إلى البيت. النهاية."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Every great match is a great story. Today, YOU are the writer!","on_screen":"A Match to Remember 🏆","visual":"Omar opens a storybook; a stadium pops up from the pages."},{"time":"00:20–01:00","narration":"Pick a card: The New Player, The Big Comeback, The Lost Goggles or Wind on the Beach.","on_screen":"Setting · Characters · Problem","visual":"Four cards spin and show their sports."},{"time":"01:00–01:45","narration":"Plan with the Story Map: beginning, problem, events, exciting moment, ending.","on_screen":"Story Map 🗺️","visual":"A path across a map lights up from Start to Finish."},{"time":"01:45–02:35","narration":"\"It's no use,\" Faisal said… \"Stop trying to win alone and start passing.\"","on_screen":"Dialogue + action","visual":"The basketball comeback story is animated with quotation marks glowing."},{"time":"02:35–03:00","narration":"End with what you learned. Then edit, publish and share your story!","on_screen":"The class storybook 📚","visual":"Pages fly into a class book titled 'Matches to Remember'."}],"captions_ar":["كل مباراة عظيمة قصة عظيمة. اليوم أنت الكاتب!","اختر بطاقة: اللاعب الجديد، العودة الكبيرة، نظارات السباحة، أو الريح على الشاطئ.","خطّط بخريطة القصة: البداية، المشكلة، الأحداث، اللحظة المثيرة، النهاية.","«لا فائدة»، قال فيصل… «توقفوا عن محاولة الفوز وحدكم وابدؤوا بالتمرير».","اختم بما تعلّمته، ثم دقّق وانشر قصتك وشاركها!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, exciting male sports-story voice, speed 0.90. Omar introduces the cards."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Story Starter Cards","body":"**Card A – The New Player** · Sport: football · Setting: the school field on a Thursday afternoon · Characters: you, your captain, a shy new student · Problem: your team needs one more player, but the new student has never played in a match\n\n**Card B – The Big Comeback** · Sport: basketball · Setting: the school sports hall · Characters: you, your best friend, the coach · Problem: at half time your team is losing by ten points, and everyone wants to give up\n\n**Card C – The Lost Goggles** · Sport: swimming relay · Setting: the swimming pool at the sports club · Characters: you, your cousin, a judge · Problem: your goggles break just before your turn\n\n**Card D – Wind on the Beach** · Sport: volleyball · Setting: the beach in Jeddah on a windy evening · Characters: you, your uncle, your family team · Problem: the wind keeps blowing the ball away, and your team starts to argue","word_count":144,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L04-U3-LS5-1","genre":"story starter cards","role":"model","difficulty":"450L–600L","glossary":[],"annotations":["Each card gives you a **setting**, **characters** and a **problem**. You decide **what happens** and **how the problem is solved**.","Tell the story in **first person** (I, we, my) – you are a character!","Use **dialogue** to show what the characters say and feel. Remember the five punctuation rules from Lesson 4."]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS5-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the Story Starter Cards and the model. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ البطاقات والنموذج واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What is the problem on Card C?","answer":"Your goggles break just before your turn.","explanation":"Card C.","explanation_ar":"انكسرت النظارات.","options":["Your team is losing by ten points.","The wind blows the ball away.","Your goggles break just before your turn.","A new student has never played."],"dok":1,"skill":"story elements","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What is the setting of Card D?","answer":"the beach in Jeddah on a windy evening","explanation":"Card D.","explanation_ar":"شاطئ جدة.","options":["the school sports hall","the swimming pool","the school field","the beach in Jeddah on a windy evening"],"dok":1,"skill":"setting","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"In the model, what was the score at half time?","answer":"20–10","explanation":"Model.","explanation_ar":"20–10.","options":["30–30","20–10","10–10","2–1"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What advice did Coach Saad give?","answer":"Stop trying to win alone and start passing.","explanation":"Model.","explanation_ar":"توقفوا عن اللعب الفردي ومرّروا.","options":["Stop trying to win alone and start passing.","Shoot every time.","Go home and rest.","Argue with the referee."],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Why did the narrator pass to Badr instead of shooting?","answer":"Badr was free under the basket.","explanation":"Model.","explanation_ar":"لأن بدر كان حرًا.","options":["The narrator was tired.","Faisal told him to pass.","Badr was free under the basket.","The buzzer had already sounded."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What did the narrator learn?","answer":"A team is stronger than any one player.","explanation":"Ending.","explanation_ar":"الفريق أقوى من أي لاعب.","options":["Basketball is easy.","A team is stronger than any one player.","Coaches are always right.","Winning is everything."],"dok":2,"skill":"theme","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS5-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Plan the story. Choose.","instructions_ar":"خطّط للقصة: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which sentence is the BEST beginning for a story about Card A?","answer":"On Thursday afternoon, our football team needed one more player, and only the shy new student, Ziyad, was left.","explanation":"Setting + problem.","explanation_ar":"بداية جيدة.","options":["Ziyad scored the winning goal.","The end.","Football is a sport.","On Thursday afternoon, our football team needed one more player, and only the shy new student, Ziyad, was left."],"dok":2,"skill":"beginnings","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which line of dialogue shows that a character wants to give up?","answer":"\"It's no use. We can't win,\" Faisal sighed.","explanation":"Feelings through dialogue.","explanation_ar":"يريد الاستسلام.","options":["\"It's no use. We can't win,\" Faisal sighed.","\"Pass it to me!\" Badr shouted.","\"We did it!\" we cheered.","\"Let's warm up,\" said the coach."],"dok":2,"skill":"dialogue","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which transition BEST builds excitement near the end of a match?","answer":"With ten seconds left,","explanation":"Time + tension.","explanation_ar":"With ten seconds left.","options":["Once upon a time,","With ten seconds left,","First,","The next morning,"],"dok":2,"skill":"transitions","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence keeps the FIRST-person point of view?","answer":"I threw the ball to Badr.","explanation":"I.","explanation_ar":"بضمير المتكلم.","options":["I threw the ball to Badr.","He threw the ball to Badr.","The narrator threw the ball.","They threw the ball."],"dok":1,"skill":"point of view","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which line about the volleyball team is punctuated correctly?","answer":"\"Stop arguing,\" my uncle said. \"Let's work together.\"","explanation":"Split quote, two sentences.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["\"Stop arguing\" my uncle said \"let's work together.\"","\"Stop arguing,\" my uncle said, \"Let's work together\".","\"Stop arguing,\" my uncle said. \"Let's work together.\"","Stop arguing, \"my uncle said.\""],"dok":3,"skill":"dialogue punctuation","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which is the strongest ending for a story about the lost goggles?","answer":"I swam with my eyes almost closed, and we still won a medal – I learned to stay calm when things go wrong.","explanation":"Solution + lesson.","explanation_ar":"نهاية قوية.","options":["Then I went home. The end.","My goggles were blue.","I swam with my eyes almost closed, and we still won a medal – I learned to stay calm when things go wrong.","Swimming pools have water."],"dok":3,"skill":"endings","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS5-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Plan your story with the Story Map.","instructions_ar":"خطط لقصتك بخريطة القصة.","items":[{"q":"Beginning – the setting and the characters of your sports story.","answer":"the swimming pool at the sports club; me, my cousin Hamza and a judge","explanation":"Setting + characters.","explanation_ar":"المكان + الشخصيات.","dok":1,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Problem – what goes wrong in your story?","answer":"My goggles broke just before my turn in the relay.","explanation":"Problem.","explanation_ar":"المشكلة.","dok":1,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Middle and exciting moment – two events and one line of dialogue.","answer":"Hamza said, \"Swim anyway – you can do it!\" I jumped in with no goggles. I touched the wall just before the other swimmer.","explanation":"Events + dialogue.","explanation_ar":"أحداث + حوار.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Ending – the solution and what you learned.","answer":"We won the silver medal, and I learned to stay calm when things go wrong.","explanation":"Solution + lesson.","explanation_ar":"الحل + الدرس.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS5-A4","type":"writing","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write, revise, edit and publish your story.","instructions_ar":"اكتب قصتك وحسّنها ودققها وانشرها.","items":[{"q":"Write your beginning: the setting, the characters and the problem.","answer":"On a windy evening at the beach in Jeddah, my family played volleyball against our cousins. The wind kept blowing the ball away, and soon my team started to argue.","explanation":"Beginning.","explanation_ar":"البداية.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write the middle of your story with two lines of dialogue.","answer":"\"It's your fault!\" my brother shouted. My uncle held up his hands. \"Stop arguing,\" he said calmly. \"Let's hit the ball low, under the wind.\"","explanation":"Middle + dialogue.","explanation_ar":"الوسط + حوار.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write your exciting moment and your ending with a lesson.","answer":"With one point left, I hit the ball low and fast, and it landed inside the line. We won, and I learned that a team that listens is a team that wins.","explanation":"Climax + ending.","explanation_ar":"الذروة + النهاية.","dok":3,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write one dialogue line you corrected after the Two-Partner Edit (before → after).","answer":"Before: \"Stop arguing\" my uncle said. After: \"Stop arguing,\" my uncle said.","explanation":"Editing.","explanation_ar":"تدقيق.","dok":2,"skill":"editing","stage":"production","_w":{"checklist":[],"min":null,"max":null}}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS5-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Story Map","instructions":"Organizer: Use your story card. Write short notes for each part of your story.","items":[{"q":"Beginning – setting and characters","answer":"the school sports hall at half time; me, my best friend Faisal, Coach Saad, Badr"},{"q":"Problem","answer":"losing 20–10; Faisal wants to give up – 'It's no use.'"},{"q":"Middle – events (with one line of dialogue)","answer":"Coach: 'Stop trying to win alone and start passing.' We pass; the score changes"},{"q":"Exciting moment","answer":"ten seconds left, 30–30; Faisal: 'Take the shot!' – but Badr is free"},{"q":"Ending – solution and what I learned","answer":"I pass to Badr; he scores before the buzzer; a team is stronger than one player"}]},{"id":"RW-L04-U3-LS5-WR","type":"writing","instructions":"Writing: Choose a Story Starter Card. Write a story paragraph called 'A Match to Remember' (8–10 sentences) in first person. Include a beginning with the setting and the problem, at least three lines of dialogue, an exciting moment and an ending that tells what you learned. Choose a Story Starter Card. Write a story paragraph called 'A Match to Remember' (8–10 sentences) in first person. Include a beginning with the setting and the problem, at least three lines of dialogue, an exciting moment and an ending that tells what you learned.","instructions_ar":"اختر بطاقة بداية قصة، واكتب فقرة قصصية بعنوان «مباراة لا تُنسى» (8–10 جمل) بضمير المتكلم، فيها بداية تذكر المكان والمشكلة، وثلاثة أسطر حوار على الأقل، ولحظة مثيرة، ونهاية تذكر ما تعلّمته.","prompt":"Choose a Story Starter Card. Write a story paragraph called 'A Match to Remember' (8–10 sentences) in first person. Include a beginning with the setting and the problem, at least three lines of dialogue, an exciting moment and an ending that tells what you learned.","checklist":["My beginning tells the setting, the characters and the problem.","I wrote in first person (I, we, my) all the way through.","I used at least three lines of dialogue.","I put commas and end marks inside the quotation marks.","I started a new line for each new speaker.","I used time transitions (At half time, In the second half, Finally).","My ending solves the problem and tells what I learned.","I checked capital letters, past-tense verbs and spelling."],"rubric_id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","min_words":100,"max_words":200,"organizer":"Story Map (beginning – problem – middle events – exciting moment – ending and lesson)","items":[{"q":"Choose a Story Starter Card. Write a story paragraph called 'A Match to Remember' (8–10 sentences) in first person. Include a beginning with the setting and the problem, at least three lines of dialogue, an exciting moment and an ending that tells what you learned.","answer":"At half time, our basketball team was losing 20–10, and the sports hall felt very hot. My best friend Faisal threw his water bottle onto the bench. \"It's no use,\" he said. \"They're too fast for us.\" Coach Saad looked at each of us. \"You're not playing as a team,\" he said calmly. \"Stop trying to win alone and start passing.\" In the second half, we listened. I passed to Faisal, Faisal passed to Badr, and Badr scored. Slowly, the numbers on the scoreboard changed, and with ten seconds left, the score was 30–30. \"Take the shot!\" Faisal shouted, but I saw that Badr was free under the basket. I threw him the ball, and he scored just before the buzzer. \"We did it!\" we cheered together. I will never forget that match because I learned that a team is stronger than any one player.","_w":{"checklist":["My beginning tells the setting, the characters and the problem.","I wrote in first person (I, we, my) all the way through.","I used at least three lines of dialogue.","I put commas and end marks inside the quotation marks.","I started a new line for each new speaker.","I used time transitions (At half time, In the second half, Finally).","My ending solves the problem and tells what I learned.","I checked capital letters, past-tense verbs and spelling."],"min":100,"max":200}}]}],"game":{"name":"Story Map Relay","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Relay story: four runners on a track each hold one part of the Story Map; the child chooses the best sentence for each part and passes the baton. A complete, well-ordered story crosses the finish line and earns a medal.","Each team gets one Story Starter Card and a Story Map poster.","Runner 1 writes the beginning and passes the baton.","Runner 2 writes the problem with one line of dialogue; Runner 3 writes the exciting moment; Runner 4 writes the ending.","Teams read their story aloud.","Points: clear problem = 2, correct dialogue punctuation = 2, a lesson in the ending = 2."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What does a story's *setting* tell you?","answer":"where and when the story happens","explanation":"Setting.","explanation_ar":"المكان والزمان.","options":["who wins","the lesson","where and when the story happens","the title only"],"dok":1,"skill":"story elements"},{"q":"A losing team that starts winning again makes a ___.","answer":"comeback","explanation":"Comeback.","explanation_ar":"عودة.","options":["buzzer","comeback","setting","trophy"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"*The coach spoke **calmly**.* How did he speak?","answer":"in a quiet, relaxed way","explanation":"Calmly.","explanation_ar":"بهدوء.","options":["very angrily","very fast","in a whisper only","in a quiet, relaxed way"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"What should the BEGINNING of your story include?","answer":"the setting, the characters and the problem","explanation":"Beginning.","explanation_ar":"المكان والشخصيات والمشكلة.","options":["only the ending","the lesson","the setting, the characters and the problem","a list of rules"],"dok":1,"skill":"story structure"},{"q":"Which line from the basketball story is punctuated correctly?","answer":"\"We did it!\" we cheered together.","explanation":"! inside + small letter.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["\"We did it\"! we cheered together.","\"We did it!\" we cheered together.","\"We did it!\" We cheered together.","\"We did it!,\" we cheered together."],"dok":2,"skill":"dialogue punctuation"},{"q":"Which sentence is in FIRST person?","answer":"My best friend Faisal threw his bottle.","explanation":"My.","explanation_ar":"بضمير المتكلم.","options":["His best friend Faisal threw his bottle.","Their friend threw a bottle.","The boy's friend threw a bottle.","My best friend Faisal threw his bottle."],"dok":2,"skill":"point of view"},{"q":"Why does the model story use dialogue at the turning point?","answer":"to show the coach's important advice in his own words","explanation":"Purpose.","explanation_ar":"لإظهار نصيحة المدرب بكلماته.","options":["to show the coach's important advice in his own words","to make the story shorter","to tell the score","to list the players"],"dok":2,"skill":"author's craft"},{"q":"Which order is correct for a story?","answer":"beginning → problem → events → exciting moment → ending","explanation":"Story Map.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الصحيح.","options":["ending → beginning → problem","exciting moment → beginning → ending","problem → ending → beginning","beginning → problem → events → exciting moment → ending"],"dok":2,"skill":"story structure"},{"q":"Which ending shows what the character LEARNED?","answer":"I learned that a team is stronger than any one player.","explanation":"Lesson.","explanation_ar":"يُظهر الدرس.","options":["Then we had dinner.","I learned that a team is stronger than any one player.","The score was 32–30.","The hall was hot."],"dok":3,"skill":"endings"},{"q":"Why is *Then I went home. The end.* a weak ending?","answer":"It has no feeling, solution or lesson.","explanation":"Weak ending.","explanation_ar":"بلا شعور أو درس.","options":["It has no feeling, solution or lesson.","It is too long.","It uses dialogue.","It is in first person."],"dok":3,"skill":"evaluate"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'setting': a sports hall with a clock on the wall"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'comeback': a scoreboard changing from 10–20 to 30–30"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'goggles': swimming goggles"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'argue': two children arguing"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'buzzer': a scoreboard with a buzzer"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'calmly': a relaxed coach talking to players"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'unforgettable': a child holding a photo of a match"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-01","prompt":"A class storybook of sports stories."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-02","prompt":"Four story starter cards."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L04-U3-LS5-03","prompt":"A story map shaped like a path to a trophy."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V01","script":"setting. The setting is the sports hall."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V02","script":"comeback. Our team made a big comeback."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V03","script":"goggles. My goggles broke before the race."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V04","script":"argue. The players started to argue."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V05","script":"buzzer. He scored just before the buzzer."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V06","script":"calmly. The coach spoke calmly."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-V07","script":"unforgettable. It was an unforgettable match."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-T1","script":"**Card A – The New Player** · Sport: football · Setting: the school field on a Thursday afternoon · Characters: you, your captain, a shy new student · Problem: your team needs one more player, but the new student has never played in a match **Card B – The Big Comeback** · Sport: basketball · Setting: the school sports hall · Characters: you, your best friend, the coach · Problem: at half time your team is losing by ten points, and everyone wants to give up **Card C – The Lost Goggles** · Sport: swimming relay · Setting: the swimming pool at the sports club · Characters: you, your cousin, a judge · Problem: your goggles break just before your turn **Card D – Wind on the Beach** · Sport: volleyball · Setting: the beach in Jeddah on a windy evening · Characters: you, your uncle, your family team · Problem: the wind keeps blowing the ball away, and your team starts to argue"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L04-U3-LS5-VID","script":"Every great match is a great story. Today, YOU are the writer! Pick a card: The New Player, The Big Comeback, The Lost Goggles or Wind on the Beach. Plan with the Story Map: beginning, problem, events, exciting moment, ending. \"It's no use,\" Faisal said… \"Stop trying to win alone and start passing.\" End with what you learned. Then edit, publish and share your story!"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Mr. Saad blows his whistle and shows the players how to pass. He is the team's ___.","answer":"coach","explanation":"Coach.","explanation_ar":"المدرب.","options":["trophy","goal","crowd","coach"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Hamza wears the armband and leads the team. He is the ___.","answer":"captain","explanation":"Captain.","explanation_ar":"القائد.","options":["referee","judge","captain","narrator"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"The swimmers ___ every morning before school to get faster.","answer":"train","explanation":"Train.","explanation_ar":"يتدرّبون.","options":["train","cheer","argue","score"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*The team didn't win, but the coach was proud of their **effort**.* *Effort* means ___.","answer":"hard work","explanation":"Effort.","explanation_ar":"الجهد.","options":["a gold cup","a loud noise","a short break","hard work"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"After the match, both teams shook hands to show ___.","answer":"respect","explanation":"Respect.","explanation_ar":"الاحترام.","options":["goggles","respect","a penalty","a buzzer"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*After the race, the runners walked slowly to ___.*","answer":"cool down","explanation":"After sport.","explanation_ar":"التهدئة.","options":["warm up","cool down","kick off","give up"],"dok":2,"skill":"phrasal verbs","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*The players **cooperated** to build the human pyramid.* *Cooperated* means ___.","answer":"worked together","explanation":"Cooperate.","explanation_ar":"تعاونوا.","options":["argued","gave up","worked together","went home"],"dok":2,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Our school won every match this year. We are the ___!","answer":"champions","explanation":"Champion.","explanation_ar":"الأبطال.","options":["champions","coaches","referees","judges"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which line from Adam's race is punctuated correctly?","answer":"\"I think so,\" I answered quietly.","explanation":"Comma inside.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["\"I think so,\" I answered quietly.","\"I think so\", I answered quietly.","\"I think so.\" I answered quietly.","I think so, \"I answered quietly.\""],"dok":1,"skill":"dialogue punctuation","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence with the speaker tag FIRST is correct?","answer":"Mr. Khalid asked, \"Are you ready, Adam?\"","explanation":"Comma + capital + ? inside.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["Mr. Khalid asked \"are you ready, Adam?\"","Mr. Khalid asked, \"Are you ready, Adam\"?","Mr. Khalid asked, \"Are you ready, Adam?\"","Mr. Khalid asked. \"Are you ready, Adam?\""],"dok":2,"skill":"dialogue punctuation","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence about the race needs quotation marks?","answer":"Layla shouted, Come on, Adam!","explanation":"Exact words.","explanation_ar":"تحتاج علامات تنصيص.","options":["Layla told Adam to keep going.","Layla said that Adam was fast.","Layla cheered for Adam from the stands.","Layla shouted, Come on, Adam!"],"dok":2,"skill":"direct speech","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Change to THIRD person: *I crossed the finish line.*","answer":"Adam crossed the finish line.","explanation":"I → Adam / he.","explanation_ar":"ضمير الغائب.","options":["I crossed the finish line.","We crossed the finish line.","Adam crossed the finish line.","My crossed the finish line."],"dok":1,"skill":"point of view","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which is the BEST beginning for a story called *The Day I Didn't Give Up*?","answer":"On the morning of the school swimming race, my goggles broke, and my race was only five minutes away.","explanation":"Setting + problem.","explanation_ar":"بداية جيدة.","options":["I won the race.","On the morning of the school swimming race, my goggles broke, and my race was only five minutes away.","Swimming is a sport.","The end."],"dok":2,"skill":"beginnings","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"},{"q":"Which ending shows what the writer LEARNED?","answer":"I didn't win, but I learned that finishing a race is a victory too.","explanation":"Lesson.","explanation_ar":"الدرس.","options":["Then I ate lunch.","The pool was blue.","There were six swimmers.","I didn't win, but I learned that finishing a race is a victory too."],"dok":3,"skill":"endings","_part":"Part D – Writing skills"}],"unit_writing":{"task":"Write a story paragraph (8–10 sentences) called 'The Day I Didn't Give Up'. Write in first person. Include the setting, a problem, at least three lines of correctly punctuated dialogue, an exciting moment and an ending that tells what you learned.","model":"On the morning of the school swimming race, my goggles broke, and my race was only five minutes away. \"What am I going to do?\" I asked my cousin Hamza. \"Swim anyway,\" he said. \"You've trained for weeks, and you can do it.\" When the whistle blew, I jumped into the cool water with my eyes almost closed. Halfway down the pool, I felt tired, and I wanted to stop. Then I heard my team shouting, \"Keep going! Don't give up!\" I kicked harder and pulled with my arms until my hand touched the wall. I didn't come first, but I came third, and my team cheered louder than ever. That day, I learned that finishing a race is a victory too.","marks":20}});
